1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marie Duèze married Pierre Via or of life, bourgeois, consul of Cahors in 13094. From this union three children were born: Jacques of Via (appointed cardinal in 1316, he died in 1317), Arnaud de Via (named cardinal
2 CONC  in 1317) and Pierre II of Via the life or.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter II of Via or La Vie is an officer of mouth to the papal court of Avignon, Lord of Villemur in 1318 and Calvinet (CAI) in the diocese of Saint-flour. He died 28 July 1337. He married Bernardé Delmas9 were born seven children,
2 CONC  including Arnaud de La life de Villemur (c. 1305-1382) and Marie de La life de Villemur.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary in the life of Villemur (Cahors in 1315 - 28 September 1383) Avignon June 14, 1333 (in Julian calendar) Béraud Ier, wife of Auvergne, count of Clermont, 7e dauphin of Auvergne in 1351, Lord of Mercœur in 1339, died 27 August 
2 CONC 13564. By this marriage, she became "the strain" of many Royal families in Europe10.
