1 NAME Renaud V /de Pons/ Vicomte de Turenne et de Carlat
2 GIVN Renaud V
2 SURN de Pons
2 NSFX Vicomte de Turenne et de Carlat
2 _MARNM de Pons
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1320
1 DEAT
2 DATE 19 SEP 1356
2 PLAC Maupertuis
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Capitaine pour le Roi aux pays du Périgord et du Limousin.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00042084&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY Renaud V de Pons, vicomte de Turenne et de Carlat, was born about 1330, the son of Renaud IV de Pons, seigneur de Blaye, Riberac, vicomte de Turenne, and Jeanne d'Albret. With his wife, a daughter of Guillaume Flotte, se
2 CONC igneur de Revel, chancellor of France, and Alix de Mello, he had at least two sons, of whom Renaud VI would have progeny and Helie would become bishop of Angoulême.
2 CONT
2 CONT Renaud was the king's lieutenant in Perigord and Limousin. Before joining the army in 1356 he designated the lords Aimeric de La Roche, Jean Le Meingre, Guillaume de Vassal and Aimar de Polignac (from the Saintonge) as administrat
2 CONC ors for his son Renaud VI.
2 CONT
2 CONT Renaud was killed with his father at the Battle of Poitiers on 19 December 1356.
2 CONT --------------------
