1 NAME Hardouin IX /de Maillé/ baron de Maillé
2 GIVN Hardouin IX
2 SURN de Maillé
2 NSFX baron de Maillé
2 _MARNM de Maillé
1 NAME Hardouin IX, baron de Maillé
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1420
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1487
1 OCCU Chambellan de Louis XI
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00050826&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY Hardouin was the son of Hardouin VIII, baron de Maillé, and Perrinelle d'Amboise, dame de Fontenay. On 26 November 1458 he married Antoinette de Chauvigny, daughter of Guy de Chauvigny, baron de Châteauroux, and Catherin
2 CONC e de Laval. They had six children, of whom François and Hardouin X would have progeny. Antoinette died in 1473, and on 21 April 1475 Hardouin married Marguerite de La Rochefoucauld, dame de Barbezieux, widow of Jean I de La Rochef
2 CONC oucauld, seigneur et baron de La Rochefoucauld, and daughter of Jean de La Rochefoucauld, seigneur de Barbezieux et de Verteuil, and Jeanne Sanglier, dame de Château-Guibert. The marriage did not result in progeny. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hardouin was counsellor and chamberlain to Louis XI, king of France, seneschal of Santoigne, and captain of Mante. By contract of 15 February 1463, he sold the land of Montils-lez-Tours to the king. In 1475 and 1476 he rendered ho
2 CONC mage for the lands of Barbezieux and Verteuil on behalf of his second wife. In July 1486 he founded the religious chapter of Maillé. He died in 1487.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/GVLV-RLB
