2 CONT After the death of Aymer, the territory did not pass to Aymer's daughter, Isabella of Angoulême, Queen consort to John of England, but rather to the daughter of Wulgrim III, Mathilde of Angoulême, who had married Hugh IX of Lusign
2 CONC an, father of Hugh X of Lusignan.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wulgrin_II_of_Angoul%C3%AAme
2 CONT
2 CONT Wulgrin II (...) he married Pontia de la Marche (or de Montgomery), daughter of Roger the Poitevin and Almodis, the daughter of count Aldebert II of La Marche. They had only one son, William IV Taillefer.
2 CONT
2 CONT B: Abt 1134
2 CONT
2 CONT Of, Angouleme, Charente, France
2 CONT
2 CONT D: 7 Aug 1187
2 CONT
2 CONT , Messina, Sicily, Italy
2 CONT
2 CONT M: Bef 1160
2 CONT
2 CONT He was apparently poisoned by his step-daughter. There are some discrepancies about when he died in the histories.
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte d'Angoulême
2 CONT
2 CONT Died while on a crusade.
2 CONT
2 CONT William was the Count of Angoulême from 1181 to 1186.
