1 NAME Archambaud /de Comborn/ VII
2 GIVN Archambaud
2 NSFX VII
2 _MARNM de Comborn
1 NAME Archambaud VII Vicomte de Comborn
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1220
2 PLAC France
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1278
1 OCCU Vicomte de Comborn
1 TITL Vicomte
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LIMOUSIN.htm#ArchambaudVIIdied1277 '''From Medlands:''']
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ARCHAMBAUD [VII] de Comborn''', son of BERNARD [II] Vicomte de Comborn & his wife Marguerite de Turenne (-1277).  A late-13th/early 14th century monument names "dominus Archambaldus vicecomes de Combornio et dominus Bernardus f
2 CONC ilius eius et dominus Archambaldus filius domini Bernardi et domina Margarita mater dicti domini Archambaldi et dominus Guido filius domini Archambaldi"[152].  Vicomte de Comborn.  A monumental inscription records the deaths of “d
2 CONC ominus Archambaldus vicecomes de Combornio et dominus Bernardus filius eius et dominus Archambaldus filius domini Bernardi et domina Margarita mater dicti domini Archambaldi et dominus Guido filius domini Archambaldi”[153]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly MARIE de Limoges, daughter of GUY [V] Vicomte de Limoges & his [second wife Ermengarde ---].  "Gui vicomte de Limoges" confirmed his previous donations to Notre-Dame de Dalon and those of "sa…mère Ermenjart", and adds a 
2 CONC donation for the soul of "sa sœur Marie", by charter dated 29 Jul 1249[154].  An anonymous Chronicon of Saint-Marcial records that "Maria, sorore Guidonis, vicecomitis Lemovicensis" married "Archambladus vicecomes Comborum", when 
2 CONC recording the death of the latter in 1277 and the succession of "Guido primogenitus suus"[155]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly (contract 12 Jan 1256) MARGUERITE de Pons, daughter of GEOFFROY [III] Seigneur de Pons et de Montignac & his wife --- (-after 12 Nov 1306). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Archambaud [VII] & his first wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         GUY de Comborn (-before 1284).  An anonymous Chronicon of Saint-Marcial records that "Maria, sorore Guidonis, vicecomitis Lemovicensis" married "Archambladus vicecomes Comborum", when recording the death of the latter i
2 CONC n 1277 and the succession of "Guido primogenitus suus"[156].  Vicomte de Comborn.  m firstly (before 1277) AMICE de Chabanais, daughter of ESCHIVAT de Chabanais & his wife ---.  An anonymous Chronicon of Saint-Marcial records that
2 CONC  "Archambladus vicecomes Comborum...Guido primogenitus suus" married firstly "Amissiam filiam Echivati de Cabanisio" during the lifetime of his father and after her death "Almodiam filiam Gaufredi de Thouvaz"[157].  m secondly ALM
2 CONC ODIS de Thouars, daughter of GEOFFROY de Thouars & his wife Marguerite de Tonnay-Charente.  An anonymous Chronicon of Saint-Marcial records that "Archambladus vicecomes Comborum...Guido primogenitus suus" married firstly "Amissiam
2 CONC  filiam Echivati de Cabanisio" during the lifetime of his father and after her death "Almodiam filiam Gaufredi de Thouvaz"[158].  Guy & his second wife had two children:  a)         EUSTACHIE de Comborn (-[Feb 1298/23 Jan 1303]). 
2 CONC  Vicomtesse de Comborn.  m as his first wife, ESCHIVARD [IV] de Preuilly Seigneur de Preuilly, son of GEOFFROY [V] Seigneur de Preuilly & his wife Marguerite --- (-1320).  Vicomte de Comborn.  b)         MARIE de Comborn (-after 4
2 CONC  Apr 1336).  Dame de Treignac.  m GUICHARD de Comborn Seigneur de Chamberet, son of HELIE de Comborn Seigneur de Chamberet & his wife Souveraine d’Aurillac (-[6 Jun 1319/19 Jan 1320]). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         BRUNISSENDE de Comborn (-after 23 Aug 1295, bur Thiern Saint-Genese).  Dame de Peschadoires et de Volore.  The testament of "Brunicendis de Combornio domina Thierni et de Piscatoriis" is dated 23 Aug 1295 and names as h
2 CONC er heirs "Guidonem dominum Thierni et Chatardum præpositum eiusdem loci liberos meos et Margaritam dominam de Buisseto filiam meam" and chooses burial "in ecclesia sancti Genesii Thiernensis, ubi est corpus domini Chatardi domini 
2 CONC de Thierno quondam mariti mei"[159].  m as his second wife, CHATARD Seigneur de Thiern, son of GUY [VI] Seigneur de Thiern & his wife Marquise de Forez (-before 1295, bur Thiern Saint-Genese). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Archambaud [VIII] & his second wife had children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         BERNARD [III] de Comborn (-[15 May/3 Dec] 1320).  Seigneur de Beaumont.  Vicomte de Comborn 1313.  m BLANCHE de Ventadour, daughter of EBLES de Ventadour Seigneur de Douzenac & his wife Galiène de Malemort (-after 1334)
2 CONC .  Bernard [III] & his wife had children:  a)         ARCHAMBAUD [VIII] de Comborn (-[1367/20 Mar 1368]).  Vicomte de Comborn 1334.  m ---.  The name of Archambaud’s wife is not known.  Archambaud [VIII] & his wife had children:  
2 CONC i)          ARCHAMBAUD [IX] de Comborn ([1331]-after 15 Mar 1380).  Vicomte de Comborn.  He sold Comborn in 1379 to his cousin Guichard de Comborn Seigneur de Treignac.  m (contract 13 Nov 1341) MARIE de Chalus-Marche, daughter of
2 CONC  AMBLARD de Chalus-Marche & his wife Agnes de Naillac (-after 20 Mar 1368). 
2 CONT
