1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Barbe Cauchon ° ~1526 + après 04/09/1577 (testament à Pujols)
2 CONT dame de Maupas, fille d’honneur de la Reine Eléonore d’Autriche
2 CONT (réputé des plus jolies de la Cour, & dotée en 1538 de 14.000 £ par le Roi)
2 CONT ép.1) 16/01/1538 Symphorien de Durfort, seigneur de Duras,
2 CONT Gentilhomme ordinaire de la Chambre du Roi, colonel
2 CONT des légionnaires de Guyenne ° ~1523 +X 12/03/1563 (Orléans)
2 CONT ép. 2) Gui 1er Chabot, baron de Jarnac, seigneur de Saint-Gelais,
2 CONT Montlieu, Saint-Aulaye et Longchamp ° ~1509 + après 06/08/1584
2 CONT Gouverneur de la Rochelle & du Pays d’Aunis, Sénéchal du Périgord
2 CONT [http://racineshistoire.free.fr/LGN/PDF/Cauchon.pdf]
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT https://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00024668&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY Barbe Cauchon de Maupas was born about 1525, the daughter of Thierry Cauchon, seigneur de Maupas, and Adrienne Bossut-Longueval. Her father was governor of Reims. Barbe married Symphorien de Durfort, seigneur de Duras, s
2 CONC on of François de Durfort, seigneur de Rauzan, and Catherine de Gontaut, dame de Mirambeau. They had six children, of whom three would have progeny: their second son Jacques, and their daughters Marguerite and Jeanne. Symphorien w
2 CONC as killed on 12 March 1562 at the Battle of Orléans. After 1563 she married Gui I Chabot de Saint-Gelais, baron de Jarnac, but this marriage remained childless. She died after 4 September 1577, the date of her will.
