1 NAME Sébastien /de Marillac/
2 GIVN Sébastien
2 SURN de Marillac
2 _MARNM de Marillac
1 NAME Sébastien de Marillac, Chevalier De Marillac de La Vastrie et de Lastic (l'Astricq)
1 SEX M
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} La Vie P487 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord of Lastic (l'Astricq) Chevalier Lord De Marillac and La Vastrie.
2 CONT
2 CONT Intendant, Maitre d'Hotel
2 CONT
2 CONT P488 - Sebastian had originally been a monk at Brioud, (a city in the Auvergne, today haut Loire) his elder brother's death forcing him, at age 22, to enter the lay world.
2 CONT
2 CONT The house of Lastic, with whom the family of de Marillac was to be associated, supplied canons to the priory of Brioud from at least the early 13th Century and did homage for one of their lands to the prior of St Flour, Brious in 
2 CONC 1270.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sebastian was knighted by Jean de Beuil after a combat with Amaury de Montferrand. (100 Years war)
2 CONT
2 CONT His testament is dated 3 March 1399. He is interred in the church of La Vastrie near his parents.
2 CONT
2 CONT He made his will in 1399.  (Il fit son testament in 1399). Sebastian and Antoinette had four children
