2 DATE BET 1341 AND 1349
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 1405
1 OCCU
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT From "The Mortimer Family of Wigmore: An outline lineage" by Ian Mortimer, Version 3.0, 16 June 2016 < [https://www.mortimer.co.uk/family/outlinelineage.pdf PDF] >. Page 46.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Geoffrey Mortimer (d. 1372x76), lord of Couhé, France. He played a vital political role alongside his father in the years 1328-30, and was arrested along with him in October 1330. He was not executed, however, but exiled for life
2 CONC . He removed himself to the lands in France that he inherited from his grandmother, styling himself seigneur de Couhé [en Poitou]. He married Jeanne de Lezay-Lusignan and had at least three children."
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Sir Jean de Mortemer, seigneur of Couhé, who first married Indie de l’Isle-Jourdain in 1366. He married secondly, in 1405, Aliénor de Périgord (d. 1434). If this is indeed the same man, he must by then have been in his twilight
2 CONC  years. By his first wife (supposedly) he had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Jean de Mortemer, seigneur of Couhé. See below.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT # "The Mortimer Family of Wigmore: An outline lineage" by Ian Mortimer, Version 3.0, 16 June 2016 < [https://www.mortimer.co.uk/family/outlinelineage.pdf PDF] >
2 CONT # https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL2.htm#RogerMortimerdied1398
2 CONT # Watson, G.W. "Geoffrey de Mortemer and his Descendants", in Selby, Walford D. (ed. v. 1-5); Keith W. (ed. v. 6-10) Murray; and H.W. Forsyth (ed. v. 11-38) Harwood. The Genealogist (New Series). (London: George Bell & Sons) p. 1-
2 CONC 16. < [https://archive.org/details/genealogis_22selb/page/n32/mode/1up?view=theater Archive.Org] >
2 CONT # https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Jean_de_Mortemer_%281%29
