1 NOTE Wulgrin II (also Vulgrin or Bougrin), called Taillifer or Rudel, was the Count of Angoulême from 1120 to his death in 1140. He was a son of Count William III and he married Pontia de la Marche, daughter of Roger the Poitevin and 
2 CONC Almodis, the daughter of count Aldebert II of La Marche. They have only one son, William IV of Angoulême. After the death of his first wife, Wulgrin remarried to Amable de Châtellerault and have three children: Fulk, Geoffrey "M
2 CONC artel" and an unnamed daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT He retook Blaye from William X of Aquitaine in 1127 and reconstructed the castle there in 1140.
2 CONT
2 CONT The troubadour Jaufré Rudel may be possibly his son or his son-in-law.
2 CONT
