2 CONT Comte Rotrou & his second wife Matilda/Maud had two daughters:  
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         PHILIPPA du Perche .  Her parentage is recorded by Orderic Vitalis[2425].  William of Tyre names her and her father (specifying that she was his only daughter) when he records her marriage[2426].  "Perticensis comes Rot
2 CONC rocus" donated property to the abbey of Sainte-Trinité de Tiron with the consent of "genere mei Helie filiique mee Philippe" by charter dated [1120] witnessed by "Juliane soror mea"[2427].  m HELIE d'Anjou Comte du Maine, son of F
2 CONC OULQUES V Comte d'Anjou & his first wife Eremburge Ctss du Maine (-15 Jan 1151).  
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         FELICIE du Perche .  The primary source which confirms her parentage has not yet been identified.  Neither Orderic Vitalis nor William of Tyre record a second daughter[2428].  
2 CONT
