2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Vulgrin [III] & his wife had one child:  a)         MATHILDE (-after 29 Aug 1233).  Painter cites a charter dated 29 Aug 1233 under which Juhel Archbishop of Tours confirmed an agreement between "Matilda daughter of Vulgrin 
2 CONC once count of Angoulême and widow of Hugh once count of La Marche" and "Isabelle queen of England, countess of La Marche and Angoulême", the former abandoning to "Isabelle and her husband Hugh de Lusignan…her rights in the county 
2 CONC of Angoulême and her dower rights in the county of La Marche" in return for an annuity[568].  m ([1200/01]) as his second wife, HUGUES [X] "le Brun" Sire de Lusignan Comte de la Marche, son of HUGUES [IX] de Lusignan & his [first]
2 CONC  wife Orengarde --- (-Damietta 5 Nov 1219). 
