2 CONC ntance for her many misdeeds. On a visit to Fontevrault her son Henry III was shocked to find her buried outside the Abbey and ordered her immediately moved inside. She was finally placed beside Henry II and Eleanor of Aquitaine. 
2 CONC Afterwards most of her many children, having few prospects in France, set sail for England and the court of their half-brother King Henry III.
