2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine de Foix (c. 1455 – died before 1494) was a French noblewoman.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a daughter of Gaston IV, Count of Foix and Eleanor of Navarre, daughter of John II of Aragón and Blanche I of Navarre.
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine married Gaston II de Foix, Count of Candale and Benauges. Their only child was Anne de Foix, who married King Ladislaus II of Bohemia and Hungary.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her niece, also Catherine, was queen of Navarre 1483 - 1513.
