1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''John of Bourbon (1381–1434) was Duke of Bourbon, from 1410 to his death and Duke of Auvergne since 1416. He was the eldest son''' of Louis II and Anne of Auvergne.[1] '''Through his mother, John inherited the Co
2 CONC unty of Forez.'''
2 CONT '''During the Armagnac–Burgundian Civil War he took sides against the Burgundians. John was captured at the Battle of Agincourt and died a prisoner in London, in spite of the payment of several ransoms, and promises to support the
2 CONC  king of England as king of France'''.[2]
2 CONT '''In 1400 in Paris, he married Marie, Duchess of Auvergne''',[3] daughter of John, Duke of Berry, who inherited the Auvergne title from her father. '''They had three sons''':
2 CONT *Charles de Bourbon (1401–1456),[3] Duke of Bourbon
2 CONT *Louis of Bourbon (1403–1412, Paris), Count of Forez
2 CONT *Louis de Bourbon (1405–1486), Count of Montpensier[3]
2 CONT '''In addition, he had two illegitimate children''':
2 CONT *Margaret, married to Rodrigo de Villandrando.[a]
2 CONT *John, bishop of Puy[3]
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT a.  Vale states Villandrando was married to a bastard daughter of the Duke of Bourbon[4]
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_I,_Duke_of_Bourbon
2 CONT '''John I'''
2 CONT '''Duke of Bourbon'''
2 CONT '''Reign	1410 – 1434'''
2 CONT '''Predecessor'''	Louis II
2 CONT '''Successor'''	Charles I
2 CONT '''Born	1381'''
2 CONT '''Died	1434 (aged 52–53)'''
2 CONT '''London'''
2 CONT '''Spouse	Marie, Duchess of Auvergne'''
2 CONT House	Bourbon
2 CONT '''Father'''	Louis II, Duke of Bourbon
2 CONT '''Mother'''	Anne of Auvergne
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_I,_Duke_of_Bourbon
2 CONT _____
2 CONT '''JEAN de Bourbon''', son of LOUIS II "le Bon" Duc de Bourbon & his wife Anne de Clermont (Mar 1381-in prison London 5 Jan 1434, bur Priory of Souvigny).  The testament of "Louis duc de Bourbonnais comte de Clermont et de Forez",
2 CONC  dated to [Apr 1390], appoints “'''son fils Jean” as his heir “sous la tutelle de sa femme, et à défaut de celle-ci sous la tutelle du duc de Bourgogne, en considération du mariage projeté entre sondit fils et la fille du duc de B
2 CONC ourgogne”[294].  Comte de Clermont [Jul 1399].  Chamberlain of France 18 Mar 1408'''.  The testament of "Louis duc de Bourbon", dated 24 Jan 1409 (N.S.), appointed “'''son fils Jean” as his heir[295].  He succeeded his father in 1
2 CONC 410 as JEAN I Duc de Bourbon.  He was captured by the English at the battle of Agincourt 1415, and remained a prisoner for the rest of his life.  Duc d'Auvergne, Comte de Montpensier 1418, by right of his wife.  "Jean duc de Bourb
2 CONC onnais et d’Auvergne comte de Forez et seigneur de Beaujeu, prisonnier des Anglais" appointed''' “son fils aîné Charles comte de Clermont” as “gouverneur de tous ses pays et seigneuries” by charter dated 25 Sep 1429[296].  The tes
2 CONC tament of "Jehan duc de Bourbonnois et d’Auvergne", dated 30 Jan [error, mistake for Dec 1433?] 1434 (N.S.), chose burial “en l’église des Cordeliers en la ville de Londres en Angleterre”[297]. 
2 CONT Betrothed (before [Apr 1390]) to BONNE de Bourgogne, daughter of PHILIPPE "le Hardi" Duke of Burgundy [Valois] & his wife Marguerite III Ctss of Flanders (1379-Arras 10 Sep 1399, bur Arras).  The testament of "Louis duc de Bourbon
2 CONC nais comte de Clermont et de Forez", dated to [Apr 1390], appoints “son fils Jean” as his heir “sous la tutelle de sa femme, et à défaut de celle-ci sous la tutelle du duc de Bourgogne, en considération du mariage projeté entre so
2 CONC ndit fils et la fille du duc de Bourgogne”[298]. 
2 CONT '''m (contract Paris 27 May 1400, in person Paris, Palais du Roi 21 Jun 1401) as her third husband, MARIE de Berry, widow firstly of LOUIS [II] de Châtillon Comte de Dunois and secondly of PHILIPPE d'Artois Comte d'Eu, daughter'''
2 CONC  of JEAN de France Duc de Berry & his first wife Jeanne d'Armagnac '''(-Lyon Jun 1434, bur Priory of Souvigny).  Père Anselme records her marriage contract dated 27 May 1400[299].  Appointed Dss d'Auvergne, Ctss de Montpensier 26 
2 CONC Apr 1418, confirmed 1425.  Her husband appointed her administrator of all his estates 17 Jan 1421 during his imprisonment.''' 
2 CONT '''Jean & his wife had three children:''' 
2 CONT 1.         CHARLES de Bourbon (1401-Château de Moulins 4 Dec 1456, bur Priory of Souvigny).  Comte de Clermont.  "Jean duc de Bourbonnais et d’Auvergne comte de Forez et seigneur de Beaujeu, prisonnier des Anglais" appointed “son 
2 CONC fils aîné Charles comte de Clermont” as “gouverneur de tous ses pays et seigneuries” by charter dated 25 Sep 1429[300].  He succeeded his father in 1434 as CHARLES I Duc de Bourbon et d'Auvergne. 
2 CONT -        see below. 
2 CONT 2.         LOUIS de Bourbon (after 24 Jan 1409-Louvres en Parisis, Val d'Oise 1412, bur Senlis, église des Cordeliers).  His date of birth is confirmed by the testament of "Louis duc de Bourbon", dated 24 Jan 1409 (N.S.), which ap
2 CONC pointed “son fils Jean” as his heir and required that “si le même Jean a second fils” he should receive “en apanage la seigneurie de Beaujolais”[301]. 
2 CONT 3.         LOUIS de Bourbon (after 1412-May 1486, bur Aigueperse, Chapelle Saint-Louis).  He was presumably born after the death of his older brother of the same name.  "Charles de Bourbon comte de Clermont fils aîné du duc de Bou
2 CONC rbonnais, agissant pour son frère Louis" and “Robert Dauphin évêque de Chartres, Jacquette Dauphine abbesse de Saint-Menoux, Bertrand seigneur de la Tour, agissant pour leur nièce et petite-fille Jeanne, fille de feu Béraud Dauphi
2 CONC n d’Auvergne” agreed the conditions for the marriage “entre lesdits Louis et Jeanne”, providing “le comté de Montpensier et la seigneurie de Beaujeu” as dowry, by charter dated 9 Oct 1426[302].  Comte de Montpensier.   
2 CONT -        see below. 
2 CONT '''Jean I had five illegitimate children by unknown mistresses:''' 
2 CONT 4.          JEAN bâtard de Bourbon (-Prieuré de Saint-Rambert en Forez 2 Dec 1485, bur Abbaye de Cluny).  Abbé de Saint-André, Villeneuve-les-Avignon 1439.  Elected Archbishop of Lyon, but renounced 6 Apr 1444.  Elected Bishop of 
2 CONC Puy, Comte de Velay 2 Dec 1443.  Administrator of the Bishopric of Lyon 1449-1470 for his nephew Charles de Bourbon.  Abbé de Cluny 1456, resigned 8 Sep 1485.  Prieur de Saint-Rambert en Forez 1468.  Prieur de Montverdun 1482.  Li
2 CONC eutenant General of Bourbon for his nephew Jean II Duc de Bourbon 6 Dec 1484[303].  
2 CONT 5.          ALEXANDRE bâtard de Bourbon (-drowned Bar-sur-Aube 15 Dec 1440).  Canon of the collégiale church of Notre-Dame de Beaujeu.  Leader of the "Ecorcheurs".  He was arrested after taking part in the revolt of the Praguerie 
2 CONC and drowned on orders of the king[304]. 
2 CONT 6.          GUY batard de Bourbon (-1442 before 18 Jun).  Père Anselme notes documents dated 1438, 6 Jun 1439 (“noble Guy bâtard de Bourbon, écuyer”), 24 Aug 1440 (appointed “capitaine et châtelain du pays et baronnie de Rouannois
2 CONC ” by Charles I Duc de Bourbon) in which he was named[305].  Père Anselme records his death “en 1442, avant le 18 de juin” (no source cited)[306]. 
2 CONT 7.          MARGUERITE bâtarde de Bourbon .  The marriage contract between "Rodrigo de Villandrando comte de Ribadeo" and “Marguerite de Bourbon sœur naturelle de Charles duc de Bourbonnais”, with “le château d’Ussel” as her dowry
2 CONC , is dated 24 May 1433[307].  m (contracts 24 May 1433, 2 Aug 1436) as his first wife, don RODRIGO de Villandrado Conde de Ribadeo, son of don PEDRO de Villandrado & his wife doña Inés de Corral (Valladolid ---- - ).  Père Anselme
2 CONC  records records biographical details, including his parentage, his career in France, his daughter by his first wife, his second marriage, and daughter by his second wife[308].  Created Conde de Ribadeo 22 Feb 1431 by Juan II King
2 CONC  of Castile.  Seigneur d'Ussel, counsellor and chamberlain of Charles VII King of France.  He returned to Castile after the death of his first wife. 
2 CONT 8.          EDMEE bâtarde de Bourbon .  Père Anselme records her parentage but provides no other details about her life (no source cited)[309]. 
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BOURBON.htm#JeanIDucdied1434B
2 CONT ____________
2 CONT '''Jean I de Bourbon, Duc de Bourbon'''1 
2 CONT M, #113653, '''b. 1380, d. 1434'''
2 CONT Last Edited=10 May 2003
2 CONT '''     Jean I de Bourbon, Duc de Bourbon was born in 1380.1 He was the son''' of Louis II de Bourbon, Duc de Bourbon and Anne de Clermont, Comtesse de Forez.2 '''He married Marie de Berry''', daughter of Jean I, Duc de Berry and 
2 CONC Jeanne d'Armagnac, '''in 1400.1 He died in 1434.'''1
2 CONT '''     He gained the title of Duc de Bourbon.'''1
2 CONT '''Children of Jean I de Bourbon, Duc de Bourbon and Marie de Berry'''
2 CONT 1. Louis I de Bourbon, Comte de Montpensier+2 d. 1486
2 CONT 2. Charles I de Bourbon, Duc de Bourbon+2 b. 1401, d. 4 Dec 1456
2 CONT Citations
