1 NAME Bertrand /de Marillac/
2 GIVN Bertrand
2 _MARNM de Marillac
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 ADDR
3 CITY Aigueperse
3 STAE Auvergne
3 CTRY France
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} AKA Sebastian I?
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertrand, Seigneur de la Vastrie. The terre of Marillac was near the city of MAURIAC in the haut Auvergne. The property was alienated by his son, (Some doubt about which one)  Sebastian ? , on 7 May 1382 in order to ransom Bertran
2 CONC d, captured in 1375 during the 100 yrs war.
2 CONT
2 CONT We learned that it was an English strategy to capture French noblemen and hold them to ransom, as a means of gaining territory during the 100 years war.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Author records that there was a chateau and noble family house which bore the name of Marillac, situated near the city of MAURIAC.  Relevant information in the cabinet de Titre confirms this information. For the ransom, the DO
2 CONC S.BL has the terre sold through Jean de Bueil to Amaury de Montferrand.
2 CONT
2 CONT Extracted from La Vie de Michel de Marillac 1560- 1632 by Nicolas leFevre, sieur de Lezeau, Transcribed and edited by Donald A Bailey ( Canadian)
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the records from Rue du Bac, the father of Sebastian was also named Sebastian, which makes one wonder if Bertrand and Sebastian I are one and the same?
2 CONT
2 CONT According to those records, he was born 1380! 
