1 NOTE {geni:about_me} so called because of his father's German connections as King of the Romans (Almain is derived from Alemagne, Germany), was the son of Richard, 1st Earl of Cornwall and Isabel Marshal.
2 CONT
2 CONT As a nephew of both Henry III and Simon de Montfort, he wavered between the two at the beginning of the Barons' War, but finally took the royalist side and was among the prisoners taken by Montfort at the Battle of Lewes (1264), w
2 CONC as held at Wallingford Castle and later released.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1268 he took the cross with his cousin Edward, who, however, sent him back from Sicily to pacify the unruly province of Gascony. Henry took the land route with Louis IX of France and Charles I of Sicily.
2 CONT
2 CONT While attending mass at Viterbo on 13 March 1271, he was attacked by his cousins Guy and Simon the younger de Montfort, sons of Simon de Montfort, 6th Earl of Leicester, and killed in revenge for the brutal deaths of their father 
2 CONC and older brother at the Battle of Evesham. The deed is mentioned by Dante Alighieri, who took it upon himself to place Guy de Montfort in the seventh circle of hell in his masterpiece, The Divine Comedy, which was written at leas
2 CONC t 40 years after Henry's death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry was buried at Hailes Abbey.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
