1 NOTE REF: Sharon Kay Penman: "The Reckoning":  In March 1271, he was inViterbo on his way back from Crusade in the Holy land with with Charlesde Anjou King of Naples, Sicily & Jerusalem & Charles's nephew PhilippeKing of France. His co
2 CONC usins Guy & Bran de Montfort & Guy's father in lawAldobrandino Aldobrandeschi Comte de Aguilla were in town to welcome thetwo sovereigns back.  Henry of Almaine had been one of Earl Simon'ssupporters but who had betrayed his uncle
2 CONC  & pledged his allegiance backto the crown.  While Henry was at Mass in the town, Guy & Bran deMontfort slew him at the altar as he begged for mercy & drug him out intothe street where Guy hacked his body into pieces.  After fleei
2 CONC ng toAldobrandeschi's castle in Sovana, the Montfort  lands & titles wereforfeit, & they were declared outlaw as well as excommunicated by thePope.
