2 CONT
2 CONT 2.      '''   Infante don PEDRO de Mallorca'''  ([1277/80?]-[1 Jul 1285/25 Sep 1303]).  Pedro III King of Aragon informed the citizens of Mallorca of the arrival of envoys, noting that “l’infant en Pere, nebot nostre, fill del rey
2 CONC  de Mallorches” would be handed over to the authorities of Mallorca, by charter dated 1 Jul 1285[693].  The wording indicates that Pedro was given as a hostage, suggesting that he was not a baby at the time (in line with the usual
2 CONC  practice as noted below under his sister Blanca).  If that is correct, he was one of his father’s older children, although maybe not the oldest as, in that case, it seems unlikely that his father would have agreed his transfer in
2 CONC  1285.  Pedro presumably died before his father’s 25 Sep 1303 charter cited below in which he was not named, maybe many years earlier as no other mention of him has been found. 
