2 PLAC Baix-sur-Rhone 
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/provvaldi.htm#AymarPoitiersdied1366
2 CONT
2 CONT a)       '''  LOUIS de Poitiers''' (1354-Baix-sur-Rhone 4 Jul 1419, bur Crest Franciscan Monastery).  Comte de Valentinois et de Diois.  "Ludovicum de Pictavia comitem Valentinensem et Diensem" and "Ludovicum de Pictavia militem d
2 CONC ominum sancti Valerii filium et heredum...quondam domini Karoli de Pictavia..." made a succession agreement dated 1416, which names "Philippi quondam fratris dicti domini Ludovici...Lanceloti filii naturalis dicti domini Comitis"[
2 CONC 1475].  The testament of "Ludovicus de Pictavia comes Valentin. et Diensis", dated 23 Jun 1419, chooses burial "in ecclesia conventus Fratrum Minorum Cristæ Diensis diocesis", and makes bequests to "consorti suæ dominæ Guillelmetæ
2 CONC  de Grueriis...Lanceloto...filio suo naturali...Margotæ, Guillelmetæ et Mariæ filiabus suis naturalibus...consanguineo et compatri suo Anthonio de Claromonte domino Monteysonis"[1476].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly CECILE de Beaufort, daughter of GUILLAUME [III] Rogier Comte de Beaufort Vicomte de Turenne & his wife Eléonore de Comminges (-1410).  A manuscript genealogy of the Beaufort family (date not specified) names “Elion
2 CONC ordim dominam de Belliloco, Margaritam dominam de Poliniaco, Ceciliam comitissam Valentin. et Diens., Ioannam dominam de Baucio et comitissam Avelini, quæ postea nupsit Guidoni de Chavigny” as the four daughters of “Guillelmus com
2 CONC es Bellifortis et vicecomes Turenæ, uxorem...Alienordim de Convenis”[1477].  An enquiry dated 1421 records that "feu Comte de Valentinois" married "messire Raimon de Tureine…la suer"[1478].  Documents dated 1404 name "Loys de Poit
2 CONC iers Comte de Valentinois et de Dioys" and "madame Cecile femme dudit comte"[1479].  An enquiry dated 1421 concerning the succession of "le Comte de Valentinois" who died in Jul 1419 records that his first wife died in 1410[1480].
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly (contracts Thonon 19 Jul 1417, and Chambéry 11 Feb 1418) GUILLEMETTE de Gruyère, daughter of RODOLPHE de Gruyère Seigneur de Montsalvens & his wife Antoinette de Salins dame de Montferrand et de Vaugrenant (-1473 
2 CONC or after).  A manuscript records the death of "Rodulphus de Grueria Comes Grueriæ" leaving "Caterina, Ioanna, Guillemeta et Antonio liberis...Rodulfi filii sui prædefuncti" and the betrothal in 1417 of "Guillelmetam" and "comite V
2 CONC alentinensi"[1481].  The testament of "Ludovicus de Pictavia comes Valentin. et Diensis", dated 23 Jun 1419, makes bequests to "consorti suæ dominæ Guillelmetæ de Grueriis..."[1482].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mistress''' (1): CATHERINE, daughter of ---.  A manuscript names "nobilem Catharinam" as mother of "Lanceloto de Pictavia bastardo Valentinensi"[1483]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT    Comte Louis & his first wife had two children: 
2 CONT   Comte Louis had six illegitimate children by Mistress (1): 
2 CONT
