1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Wikipedia 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan I of Cabrera ( Modica , Ragusa 1405 - X 1474 ) was a Catalan nobleman, viscount of Cabrera and Bas and fourth count of Modica and count of Osona .
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Bernat Joan de Cabrera and Violant de Prades .
2 CONT
2 CONT Nuptials and descendants	Modify
2 CONT
2 CONT He married in 1458 Joana de Carmain (born in 1428 in Zaragoza [1] ), who was the sister of Joan de Carmain (Viscount of Caraman) married Isabel de Foix and de Cabrera (lady of Caselsarrazin, Sault, Saradet and Marpaps ), who was a
2 CONC lso the daughter of Sança de Cabrera (sister of Bernat Joan de Cabrera ), so Joan married his aunt's daughter-in-law. They had four legitimate children:
2 CONT
2 CONT John II of Cabrera (1432-1477) the successor to the titles. Anna I de Cabrera (1435-1527). Carles de Cabrera (1438-X). Isabel de Cabrera (1443-1493). With Rafaela de Rocabertí, daughter of Pere de Rocabertí , he had in:
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan de Cabrera i Rocabertí (1450-1520), illegitimate son, married to Anna de Miquel, and in a second marriage to Anna de Montcada. He had the heir Antic de Cabrera i de Miquel, who married in 1527 Anna de Colom i Ros. [2]
