1 NAME Archambaud Janvre, seigneur de La Bou-chetière and Veuzé
2 GIVN Archambaud Janvre, seigneur de La Bou-chetière and Veuzé
1 NAME Seigneur Archambaud Janvre
1 SEX M
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://archive.org/stream/nobiliaireuniver16sainuoft#page/274/mode/2up
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Archambaud Janvre, sgr. de La Bou-chetière and Veuzé'''
2 CONT
2 CONT REF: All Huguenot Pedigrees, Vol. 1
2 CONT
2 CONT ''X. Archambaud Janvre, 4th of the name, sgr. de La Bou-chetière and Veuzé, married (lundi après la St. Barnalé, apôtre, 1242) Dlle. Pétronille de Chaunay, daur. of Guil-laume de Chaunay, sgr. de Champdenier and Javarzay. By conse
2 CONC nt of his wife he settled his seigneurie of La Bou-chetière on the monks of the Abbey of St. Maixent in 1247, before leaving for the Crusade to the Holy Land with St. Louis. In the event of his death, he charged Dame Lectice de Su
2 CONC rgères, his mother, and his wife Pétronille to release as much of this land as possible. He was killed near Mas-sourah, defending the king, 1250. In 1256 his wife, mother, and children released the fief of La Bouehetière. He left:
2 CONC  (a) Jean, who succeeds, XI.; (b) Geoffroi, who married in 1268 Dlle. Marie Chasteigner, daur. of Guillaume Chas-teigner, sgr. de Paillès; (c) Honore, mentioned in a deed of 1256.'' 
