2 CONC berti…"[106]. A charter dated to [1124/29] relating to a dispute between the abbé de Charroux and the abbesse de Fontevrault refers to a previous donation with the consent of "Almodi comitissa Charofensi ac filius eius Audeberto e
2 CONC t Bosone"[107]. The Chronicle of Saint-Maxence records that "Rotgerio comite" & his wife had two sons[108]. "Odo comes" donated property to Tulle, with the consent of "fratre meo Aldeberto", by charter dated to [1106][109]. '''Com
