2 CONT '''HUMBERGE de Limoges''' .  The Chronicon Gaufredi Vosiensis names "Guidonem, Ademarum et Guillermum…Peregrinus…filiam Margaretam…Aquiliam…Humbergam…Mariam" as children of "Ademarum" and his wife "Sarram", specifying that Humberg
2 CONC e married "Gaufredo de Lesigniaco"[712].  The chronology of Humberge’s life is difficult to determine.  However, considering the dates of her parents and the other members of this family, it appears unlikely that she was born late
2 CONC r than [1160/80].  This would suggest that she must have been the first wife of her husband and died before 1200 when he is named in a charter with another wife.  m as his [first] wife, GEOFFROY de Lusignan Seigneur de Vouvent, so
2 CONC n of HUGUES [VIII] "le Brun" Seigneur de Lusignan & his wife Bourgogne de Rancon (-1216).
