1 OCCU Count of Perche and Mortagne; fought at battle of Hastings (14 October 1066), COUNT OF PERCHE, Comte, du Perche, Sieur, de Mortagne, de Nogent-le-Rotrou, greve i Perche, Count de Mortagne et tu Perche, count
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====FMG: Normandy: [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORMANDY%20NOBILITY.htm#GeoffroyIPerchedied1100 Alençon, Averux, Evreux, Pershe]
2 CONT * [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/cfrachacha.htm#RotrouIMortagnedied1080A '''ROTROU de Châteaudun'''], son of GEOFFROY Vicomte de Châteaudun & his wife Helvis [Elisabeth] de Corbon ( –1 Mar [1080 ] )....'''m [https://fmg.ac/Proj
2 CONC ects/MedLands/NORMANDY%20NOBILITY.htm#AdeliseAlenconMRotrouIChateaudun ADELISE de Bellême]''', daughter of GUERIN [Warinus] de Bellême & his wife —–....'''Comte Rotrou & his wife had five children:''' 
2 CONT ** 1. '''GEOFFROY de Châteaudun''' (–mid-Oct 1100, bur Nogent-le-Rotrou[2201]). Orderic Vitalis names him and his father[2202]. "''Gauffridus vicecomes, Hugo vicecomes Castriduni, Rotrocus frater eius de Montfort''" witnessed a do
2 CONC nation to Saint-Denis de Nogent by "''Henricus vicecomes Mauritanie''"[2203], the charter dated to [1060] in the compilation. "''Gaufridi, Hu''[''gonis''], ''Rotroci, Fulcoisi filiorum meorum''" consented to the confirmation of do
2 CONC nations to Saint-Denis de Nogent by "''Rotrocus castri Mauritanie comes atque Dunensis castri vicecomes''" dated 11 Jan 1078[2204]. Orderic Vitalis names “...''Goifredus Rotronis Moritoniæ comitis filius''...” among those who took
2 CONC  part in the battle of Hastings[2205]. He succeeded his father in [1080] as Comte de Mortagne. "''Gaufridus castri Mauritaniæ comes''" confirmed donations to Saint-Denis de Nogent by charter dated [1080] in which he named "''avus 
2 CONC meus dominus Gaufridus vicecomes Castriduni et pater meus Rotrocus comes''"[2206]. Orderic Vitalis records that “Goisfredus Rotronis Mauritaniæ comitis filius” rebelled against Robert [III] Duke of Normandy, burnt “''Excalfoium''”
2 CONC  [Echaufour], and claimed (Orderic says with justification) “''Danfrontem...castrum''” [Domfront] from “''Rodberto cognato suo''”, dated to [1088][2207]. It appears that Geoffroy’s claim to Domfront was through his mother’s family
2 CONC , her grandfather having first constructed the castle. It is unlikely, therefore, that the claim by Duke Robert was based on a family connection: more likely Domfront had at some point been occupied by the duke or his father. This
2 CONC  leaves open the precise relationship between Geoffroy and Duke Robert “cognato suo”, which has not been traced. He '''adopted the title Comte du Perche''' after 1090. "''Hugo vicecomes de Castroduno''" donated the church of Saint
2 CONC -Léonard de Bellême to Marmoutier, with the consent of "''Gausfredo comite fratre eius, Roberto Mandaguerran fratre eius, Comitissa uxore eius, Gausfredo filio eius, Matilde filia eius''", by charter dated to [1092/1100][2208]. Hi
2 CONC s '''burial''' at Nogent-le-Rotrou is confirmed by the charter dated 1099 under which "''Rotrocus filius domini Gauffridi comitis Mauritaniensis''" confirmed donations to Saint-Denis de Nogent after returning from Jerusalem and vi
2 CONC siting his father's tomb[2209].
2 CONT ** '''m [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/chamdampjo.htm#BeatrixRoucydiedafter1129MPerche BEATRIX de Ramerupt]''', daughter of HILDUIN [IV] de Montdidier et de Ramerupt Comte de Roucy & his wife Adelaide de Roucy (-2 Sep after 112
2 CONC 9). "''Beatrice uxor mea et filio meo Rotroco nec non fratribus meis''" confirmed the confirmation of donations to Saint-Denis de Nogent by "''Gaufridus castri Mauritaniæ comes''" dated [1080][2210]. The Chronicle of Alberic de Tr
2 CONC ois-Fontaines names "''Beatrix''" as second daughter of Hilduin Comte de Roucy and incorrectly names her husband "''Rotroldo comiti de Pertico''"[2211]. The ''Genealogiæ Scriptoris Fusniacensis'' names "''comitis Hilduini de Ramer
2 CONC uth maior natu filia dicta Beatrix''" as wife, also incorrectly, of "''Rotaldo comiti de Pertica''"[2212]. She is named as wife of Geoffroy Comte du Perche by Orderic Vitalis, but this source incorrectly states that she was the da
2 CONC ughter of "the count of Rochefort"[2213], while specifying in another passage that her son Rotrou was consanguineus of Alfonso I King of Aragon[2214]. A close family relationship with the Comtes de Rochefort is nevertheless sugges
2 CONC ted by "''Rotrocus comes Perticensis, Beatrix comitissa mater eiusdem''" witnessing the charter dated [1114] under which "''Guido comes Rocheforti''" donated property to the abbey of Sainte-Trinité de Tiron[2215], although this re
2 CONC lationship has not been identified. "''Rotrocus comes et Beatrix mater eius atque Mathildis uxor comitis''" subscribed the charter dated to [1105/07] under which "Guillermus de Loiscel" made donations to Saint-Denis de Nogent[2216
2 CONC ].
2 CONT ** '''Comte Geoffroy & his wife had five children''':
2 CONT *** a) '''ROTROU "le Grand" du Perche''' (–killed in battle Rouen [20 Jan/23 Apr] or 6 May 1144)....He succeeded his father as Comte du Perche. — [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORMANDY%20NOBILITY.htm#RotrouIdied1144B '''see be
2 CONC low''']. 
2 CONT *** b) '''MARGUERITE du Perche''' (–27 Aug after 1156)....[https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL.htm#HenryBeaumontWarwickdied1119B '''m HENRY de Beaumont'''] Earl of Warwick, son of ROGER Seigneur de Beaum
2 CONC ont-le-Roger & his wife Adeline de Meulan ({1048}-20 Jun} 1119, bur Préaux). 
2 CONT *** c) '''JULIANE du Perche''' (–after 1132)....'''m''' ( [1092] ) [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORMANDY%20NOBILITY.htm#GilbertLaigleMJulianaMortagnePerche '''GILBERT Seigneur de Laigle'''], son of RICHER Seigneur de Laigle &
2 CONC  his wife Judith d'Avranches ( – [1118] ).
2 CONT *** d) MATHILDE du Perche (before 1100-27 May 1143, bur Arnaco)....'''m''' firstly [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LIMOUSIN.htm#RaymondITurennehttps://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LIMOUSIN.htm#RaymondITurenne '''RAYMOND''' [I] '''Vi
2 CONC comte de Turenne'''], son of BOSON [I] Vicomte de Turenne & his wife Gerberge —–.  1127. '''m''' secondly [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LIMOUSIN.htm#GuyLastoursMMathildePerche '''GUY''' [IV] '''"le Gros" de Lastours'''], son o
2 CONC f GERARD [I] de Lastours & his wife Humberga —– (–Jerusalem [1147/49]).
2 CONT *** e) daughter. The primary source which confirms her parentage has not yet been identified.
2 CONT <nowiki>—</nowiki>
