1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From the [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORMAN%20NOBILITY.htm#GeoffroyIPerchedied1100 FMG Medieval Lands database]:
2 CONT
2 CONT daughter of Hildouin IV de Montdidier (Ramerupt) and Adelaide de Roucy:
2 CONT
2 CONT '''BEATRIX de Ramerupt''' (-2 Sep after 1129).  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Beatrix" as second daughter of Ebles Comte de Roucy and incorrectly names her husband "Rotroldo comiti de Pertico"[1076].  The Gene
2 CONC alogiæ Scriptoris Fusniacensis names "comitis Hilduini de Rameruth maior natu filia dicta Beatrix" as wife, also incorrectly, of "Rotaldo comiti de Pertica"[1077].  She is named as wife of '''Geoffroy Comte du Perche''' by Orderic
2 CONC  Vitalis, incorrectly saying that she was daughter of "the count of Rochefort"[1078] and specifying in another passage that her son Rotrou was consanguineus of Alfonso I King of Aragon[1079].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m '''GEOFFROY de Châteaudun''', son of ROTROU Vicomte de Châteaudun, Comte de Mortagne & his wife Adelise de Bellême (-mid-Oct 1100, bur Nogent-le-Rotrou[1080]).  He succeeded his father in [1080] as '''Comte de Mortagne'''.  He a
2 CONC dopted the title '''Comte du Perche''' after 1090. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Geoffroy & his wife had five children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         ROTROU "le Grand" du Perche (-killed in battle Rouen [20 Jan/23 Apr] or 6 May 1144).  He is named and his parentage given by Orderic Vitalis[2155].  "Beatrice uxor mea et filio meo Rotroco nec non fratribus meis" confir
2 CONC med the confirmation of donations to Saint-Denis de Nogent by "Gaufridus castri Mauritaniæ comes" dated [1080][2156].  He succeeded his father as Comte du Perche. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         MARGUERITE du Perche (-27 Aug after 1156).  She is named and her parentage given in Orderic Vitalis, who also names her husband and, in a later passage, her father and two older sons[2157].  The Genealogiæ Scriptoris Fu
2 CONC sniacensis names " Rotaldum eiusdem loci comitem et Iulainam de Aquila matrem regine Navarrensis, et Margaretam uxorem Gisleberti de Novo-burgo" as children, incorrectly, of "Rotaldo comiti de Pertica" & his wife Beatrix de Roucy,
2 CONC  specifying that Marguerite had children "Rotaldum Ebrodiensem episcopum cum aliis liberis utriusque sexus"[2158].  “Henricus…Warwicense consul et Margareta uxor mea et Rogerus noster filius” donated property to Warwick St Mary by
2 CONC  undated charter[2159].  The 1130 Pipe Roll records "comitisse de Warwic" in Wiltshire[2160].  1156.  The necrology of the church of Evreux records the death "27 Aug" of "Margarita mater Rotrodi episcopi"[2161].  m HENRI de Beaumo
2 CONC nt Earl of Warwick, son of ROGER Seigneur de Beaumont-le-Roger & his wife Adeline de Meulan ([1048]-[20 Jun] 1119, bur Préaux). 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)         JULIANA du Perche (-after 1132).  She is named and her parentage given in Orderic Vitalis, who also names her husband[2162].  The Genealogiæ Scriptoris Fusniacensis names "Rotaldum eiusdem loci comitem et Iulainam de Aq
2 CONC uila matrem regine Navarrensis, et Margaretam uxorem Gisleberti de Novo-burgo" as children, incorrectly, of "Rotaldo comiti de Pertica" & his wife Beatrix de Roucy, specifying that Marguerite had children "Rotaldum Ebrodiensem epi
2 CONC scopum cum aliis liberis utriusque sexus"[2163].  "Rotrocus comes Perticensium" donated property to the abbey of Sainte-Trinité de Tiron by charter dated [1119] subscribed by "Juliane soror mea, Richerii filius eius"[2164].  "Juli
2 CONC ane soror mea" witnessed the charter dated [1120] under which "Perticensis comes Rotrocus" donated property to the abbey of Sainte-Trinité de Tiron[2165].  "Domine Juliane" recognised rights of Saint-Denis de Nogent  by charter da
2 CONC ted to [1122/33], specifying that she was governing Perche while the count was absent in Spain, witnessed by "Gislebertus puer filius prefate Juliane"[2166].  m GILBERT Seigneur de Laigle, son of RICHER de Laigle & his wife Judith
2 CONC  d'Avranches (-[1118]). 
2 CONT
2 CONT d)         MATHILDE du Perche (before 1100-27 May 1143, bur Arnaco).  The Chronicon Gaufredi Vosiensis records the marriage of "Guidonem",  son of "Gerardus", and "Matilde, matre Bosonis de Torena quæ Arnaco condita est"[2167].  I
2 CONC n another passage, the Chronicon Gaufredi Vosiensis records that "Raymundus" married "Mathilde…soror Comitis de Pertico"[2168].  The Chronicon Gaufredi Vosiensis records the death "V Kal Jun" of "Mathildis uxor quondam Raymundi de
2 CONC  Torenna" and her burial by "Guidone…Crassus viro suo filio Geraldi de Turribus" at "Arnaco", recording that her son Boson was killed within one month of his mother's death[2169].  m firstly RAYMOND [I] Vicomte de Turenne, son of 
2 CONC BOSON [I] Vicomte de Turenne & his wife Gerberge ---.  1127.  m secondly GUY [IV] "le Gros" de Lastours, son of GERARD [I] de Lastours & his wife Humberga --- (-Jerusalem [1147/49]).
2 CONT
2 CONT e)         daughter .  The primary source which confirms her parentage has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT =<nowiki>---------------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT Geoffrey du Perche et Mortaigne I, died 1100. He was the son of 12. Rotrou de Chateaudun I and 13. Adeline Domfront. He married 7. Beatrice de Montdidier.
2 CONT
2 CONT  7. Beatrice de Montdidier She was the daughter of 14. Hildouin de Montdidier and 15. Alice de Roucy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Geoffrey Mortaigne and Beatrice de Montdidier are:
2 CONT
2 CONT   i. Julienne du Perche, married Gilbert l'Aigle 1091; born Bef. 1047.
2 CONT
2 CONT  3 ii. Mahaut du Perche, born Bet. 1100 and 1105 in Perche, Normandy, France; died 18 May 1143; married Raymond de Turenne I 1122.
2 CONT
2 CONT   iii. Margaret du Perche, born Abt. 1045; died Abt. 1136; married Henry de Beaumont de Newburgh Bef. 1100 in Perche, Normandy, France; born 1045 in Neubourg, Manche, France; died 1123 in Pontaudemer, Normandy, France.
