2 CONT  JOHN I "Lackland" PLANTAGENET (King of England)
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: 24 Dec 1166, Beaumont Palace, Oxford, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Acceded: 27 May 1199, Westminster Abbey, London, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Died: 18/9 Oct 1216, Newark Castle, Newark, Nottinghamshire
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried: Worcester Cathedral
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes: Signed the Magna Carta at Runnymede, 1215. Reigned 1199-1216. His reign saw renewal of war with Phillip II Augustus of France to whom he has lost several continental possesions including Normandy by 1205. He came into confl
2 CONC ict with his Barons and was forced to Sign the Magna Carta. His later repudiation of the charter led to the first barons war 1215-17 during which John died. Burke says he was born in 1160. King of Ireland 1177, Count of Mortain 11
2 CONC 89, Earl of Gloucester. It is known that Agatha Ferrers was a mistress of John, but it is only supposition that she is the mother of Joan.
2 CONT
