2 NOTE To many cooks have distroyed this tree!
3 CONT John Lackland, King of England is my 20th great grandmother's husband's father.
2 NOTE John Lackland, King of England is my 21st great grandfather.
3 CONT
3 CONT Why is there so many duplicates? Many are not even identified.
2 NOTE In September 1216 John began a fresh, vigorous attack. He marched from the Cotswolds, feigned an offensive to relieve the besieged Windsor Castle, and attacked eastwards around London to Cambridge to separate the rebel-held areas 
3 CONC of Lincolnshire and East Anglia. From there he travelled north to relieve the rebel siege at Lincoln and back east to King's Lynn, probably to order further supplies from the continent. In King's Lynn, John contracted dysentery, w
3 CONC hich would ultimately prove fatal.
3 CONT
3 CONT Sidebar: If you ever in the England make it a point to go the Cotswolds. It is like driving in England 700 years ago. You can not build a house unless the outside looks and matches that period of time. 
