2 CONC ueen, and was determined to ensure the recognition of her rights as sovereign duchess from now on. Although her new husband exercised the ruler's powers in Brittany, he formally recognized her right to the title "Duchess of Britta
2 CONC ny" and issuing decisions in her name.
