1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_de_Foix-Lescun
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas de Foix-Lescun (died 3 March 1525), commonly known as Lescun, was a French commander during the Italian War of 1521, and the brother of Odet de Foix, Vicomte de Lautrec, André de Foix, Lord of Lesparre and Françoise de Foix
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT He accompanied King Francis I of France in the conquest of the Duchy of Milan. He helped Pope Leo X in the conquest of the Duchy of Urbino and in 1518 he was made Marshal of France. As the French governor of Milan, his severe rule
2 CONC  gained him the people's enmity, and he had to retreat to Parma until the arrival of his brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the Battle of Bicocca, he commanded the cavalry force which attempted to flank Prospero Colonna; afterwards, he assumed command of the French army and was wounded. Later he was responsible for the French withdrawal from Italy.
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought in the battle of Pavia, being wounded while he was rescuing King Francis I. He was made prisoner and subsequently died out of his wounds.
