2 CONT '''Lajos II, King of Bohemia and Hungary'''1 
2 CONT M, #112023, '''b. 1506, d. 1526'''
2 CONT Last Edited=8 Mar 2007
2 CONT Consanguinity Index=0.1%
2 CONT '''     Lajos II, King of Bohemia and Hungary was born in 1506.1 He was the son of''' Vladislav II, King of Bohemia and Hungary and Anne de Foix, Comtesse de Candale.1,2 '''He married Maria Erzherzogin von Österreich''', daughter 
2 CONC of Felipe I von Habsburg, Rey de Castilla and Juana, Reina Juana de Castilla, '''in 1522.1 He died in 1526 killed.'''1
2 CONT '''    He was a member of the House of Jagellon. He held the office of Co-regent of Hungary in 1508.3 He held the office of Co-regent of Bohemia in 1509.4 He succeeded as the King Lajos of Bohemia in 1516.2 He gained the title of 
2 CONC King Lajos II of Hungary in 1516.'''2
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT 1.[S16] Jirí Louda and Michael MacLagan, Lines of Succession: Heraldry of the Royal Families of Europe, 2nd edition (London, U.K.: Little, Brown and Company, 1999), table 80. Hereinafter cited as Lines of Succession.
2 CONT 2.[S16] Louda and MacLagan, Lines of Succession, table 87.
2 CONT 3.[S38] John Morby, Dynasties of the World: a chronological and genealogical handbook (Oxford, Oxfordshire, U.K.: Oxford University Press, 1989), page 159. Hereinafter cited as Dynasties of the World.
2 CONT 4.[S38] John Morby, Dynasties of the World, page 156.
2 CONT From: https://www.thepeerage.com/p11203.htm#i112023
