2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT -https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/AUVERGNE.htm#RobertIVAuvergnedied1194
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ROBERT [IV] d'Auvergne''', son of GUILLAUME [VIII] "le Vieux" Comte d'Auvergne & his wife Anne de Nevers (-[1194], bur Abbaye de Bouchet, near Limais).  A letter from the canons of Clermont to Louis VII King of France complaine
2 CONC d of the activities of “Willelmi maioris natu comitis atque filii eius Roberti”, undated[252].  Comte d'Auvergne et de Clermont.  A charter dated 1182 records an agreement between the abbot of Saint-Michel de Cluse, Piemonte and "
2 CONC comiti Roberto"[253].  Baluze states that Comte Robert died "environ l’an 1194" and was buried "en l’abbaye du Bouschet", reproducing an image of the tomb in which he and his wife are buried[254]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ( [1165] ) MATHILDE de Bourgogne, daughter of EUDES II Duke of Burgundy [Capet] & his wife Marie de Blois-Champagne ([1150]-22 Jul 1220, bur Abbaye de Bouchet, near Limais).  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines nam
2 CONC es "sorore ducis Burgundie" as wife of "Roberti [comitis Alvernie]" but does not name her[255].  Her birth and marriage dates are estimated approximately from the dates of her parents’ marriage, father’s death, and possible birth 
2 CONC dates of her siblings, but bearing in mind the possible marriage date of her second son.  A charter dated May 1201 records disputes between "dominum Robertum…Claromontensem episcopum et Guidonem…comitem Arverniæ", mediated by "dom
2 CONC ino Odone…duce Burgundiæ" and naming "domina Mathildis mater eius"[256].  Dame de Limais, by grant as dowry.  She ceded Limais to Hervé de Nevers in Jun 1210. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Comte Robert [IV] & his wife had [six] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ROBERT [IV] d'Auvergne(-[1194], bur Abbaye de Bouchet, near Limais).''' 
2 CONT s/o GUILLAUME [VIII] "le Vieux" Comte d'Auvergne & Anne de Nevers  
2 CONT x c1165 MATHILDE de Bourgogne d/o EUDES II Duke of Burgundy [Capet] & Marie de Blois-Champagne ([1150]-22 Jul 1220, bur Abbaye de Bouchet, near Limais).  
2 CONT 1.         MARIE d’Auvergne ([1165]-after 1229, bur Lyon Dominican church) x  ([1180]) ALBERT [II] Seigneur de la Tour-du Pin, son of ALBERT [I] de la Tour & his wife --- (-1229 or after). 
2 CONT 2.         GUILLAUME [IX] (-[1195/97]).  
2 CONT 3.         GUY [II] (-1222, bur Le Bouchet) x  ([1180]) PETRONILLE de Chambon, daughter of AMELIUS [III] de Chambon {Puy-de-Dôme} & his wife Dalmatie --- (-after Jun 1232). 
2 CONT 4.         ROBERT d’Auvergne (-Lyon 6 Jan 1234, bur Lyon Saint-Jean).  Bishop of Clermont 1198. 
2 CONT 5.         daughter (-1210) x GUY [V] Vicomte de Limoges, son of ADEMAR [V] Vicomte de Limoges & his wife Sarah of Cornwall (-Avignon 29 Mar 1230, bur Limoges Saint-Marcial). 
2 CONT 6.         [ROBERT de Clermont ([1180/95]-[1219/Feb 1234]).
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/AUVERGNE.htm#GuillaumeVIIIAuvergnedied1162
