2 CONT -1.         '''MARIE''' (-19 May 1280).  The late 13th century genealogy by Balduinus de Avennis records that "alium Walterum Bertolt", son of "domino Waltero Bertolt advocato Macliniensi", married "Maria filia comitis Alverniæ Wi
2 CONC lelmi", adding that they had "filios…et filias"[310].  A charter dated 1238 records a peace agreement between "ducem Brabantie" and "nobilem virum Dominum Walterum Berthout", confirmed by the marriage of "dux consanguineam suam Ma
2 CONC riam primogenitam sororis suæ comitissa de Alvernia" and "Waltero Berthout primogenito Walteri Berthout predicti"[311].  An inscription in the church at Mechelen ("antiqua ecclesia majoris Begginagii Mechliniensis") records the de
2 CONC aths of its founders, 19 May 1280 of "Maria vidua D. Waltheri de Berthaut domini Machliniensis" and 25 Feb 1299 of "Sophia de Breda eius filia vidua D. Henrici domini de Breda et de Bergis"[312].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (contract 1238) WALTER [VI] Berthout Heer van Mechelen, son of WALTER [V] Berthout Heer van Mechelen & his wife Adeluye d’Enghien (-after Nov 1286). 
