1 NAME Bermond II /d'Uzès/
2 GIVN Bermond II
2 SURN d'Uzès
2 _MARNM d'Uzès
1 NAME Bermond II //
2 GIVN Bermond II
2 SURN d'Uzès
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Saint Gilles du Gard, 30800, Gard, Languedoc, FRANCE
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1180
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 3 JUN 1254
1 OCCU 5ème sire d'Uzès (30) 1209
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/toulnoreast.htm#BermondUzesdied1254
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         BERMOND [II] (-1254).  "Bermundus dominus Ucetiæ" confirmed donations to the Chartreuse de Valbonne by "pater meus R. quondam" by charter dated Jul 1212[1548].  Seigneur d’Uzès.  "Bermundus dominus Ucetiæ" donated prope
2 CONC rty "in loco...Sopiaus" to the Chartreuse de Valbonne, for the soul of "Decani fratris mei", by charter dated 1212[1549].  "Bermundus de Ucetia filius quondam Raimundi Rascacii" swore allegiance to the bishop of Uzès for property 
2 CONC "infra et extra Ucetiam civitatem" by charter dated 12 May 1215[1550].  "Bermundus dominus Ucetiæ" recognised the rights of the monastery of Valbonne, in the presence of "Guirauda uxore mea domina Ucetiæ", by charter dated 29 Dec 
2 CONC 1222[1551].  "Bermundus dominus Ucetiæ et Armasanicarum" donated property "in aquis de Iscia" by charter dated 24 Jul 1226[1552].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (before 29 Dec 1222) GERALDE de Monteil, daughter of GIRAUD Adémar Seigneur de Monteil, Vicomte de Marseille & his wife Mabile de Marseille (-after Aug 1229).  "Bermundus dominus Ucetiæ" recognised the rights of the monast
2 CONC ery of Valbonne, in the presence of "Guirauda uxore mea domina Ucetiæ", by charter dated 29 Dec 1222[1553].  “Giraud Adhémar seigneur de Montélimar” promised “à son gendre Bermond d’Uzès” to grant him “pour la dot de sa fille Géra
2 CONC lde ses droits sur les châteaux de la Valloire (Valle Aurea) et de Cossas” by charter dated Aug 1229[1554].  Bermond & his wife had children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *i)          DECAN (-after 4 Jul 1283).  Europäische Stammtafeln records his parentage[1555].  The primary source which confirms this information has not been identified.  Seigneur d’Uzès.           see below. 
