1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ANGOULEME.htm#AymarArchiacMMargueriteRochechouart '''From Medlands:'']
2 CONT
2 CONT '''AYMAR d’Archiac .  Seigneur d’Archiac.'''  m MARGUERITE de Rochechouart, daughter of [AIMERY [X] Vicomte de Rochechouart & his wife Marguerite de Limoges].  Père Anselme names “Marguerite” as the second daughter of Aimery [X] a
2 CONC nd her husband “Aymar seigneur d’Archiac”, but cites no primary source on which the information is based[975].  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.   She is not named in her su
2 CONC pposed mother’s Jul 1252 testament.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Aymar & his wife had six children (Duchesne names “Aymar, Foucaud, Guillaume et Aymery” as the brothers of Simon d’Archiac Archbishop of Vienne, and their parentage, but does not cite the corresponding primary source[976].): 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         AYMAR d’Archiac . 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         FOUCAUD d’Archiac .  m MABILE de Vivonne, daughter of GUILLAUME de Vivonne "de Fortibus" & his wife Matilda de Ferrers ([1254/55]-).  An undated writ, after the death of "William de Fortibus", names "his four daughters,
2 CONC  Joan aged 8 years and 5 weeks, viz on Wednesday the feast of St ---, Sibyl aged 6, Mabel aged 4, and --- aged 2, are his heirs" and lists manors in Dorset[977].  Henry III King of England granted, 2 Aug 1259, "the wardship of the
2 CONC  lands late of William de Fortibus" to "Ingram de Percy, Peter de Chauuvent and Imbert de Muntferaunt" and the marriages of the deceased’s four daughters, to Imbert the marriage of "one of the remaining two as he shall choose", an
2 CONC d to "Laurence son of Nicholas de Sancto Mauro…the marriage of the remaining one"[978].  Her parentage is confirmed by the Somersetshire Pleas for 15 Jul 1269 which include a record that "Aunsell de Gurnay and his wife Sibyl" warr
2 CONC anted "Emery de Roche Chaward, son of Emery de Roche Chaward, and Joan his wife, Sibyl, Mabel and Cecily, the daughters and heirs of William de Fortibus" relating to land in "Corfton"[979].  Her marriage is confimed by a petition 
2 CONC to the king dated to [1281] by "Peter de St Hillare" relating to land at Corston, Somerset which names "Aunsel de Gunney, Sibyl wife of Aunsel de Gunney, Reginald father of Aunsel de Gunney, Joan wife of Reginald de Gunney, Guy de
2 CONC  Rochicheward, Sibyl wife of Guy de Rochicheward, John de Beauchamp, Cecily wife of John de Beauchamp, Fulk de Archiake, Mabel wife of Fulk de Archiake, William de Forz"[980].  Foucaud & his wife had [one child]:  i)          [AYM
2 CONC AR d’Archiac .  A licence dated 3 Dec 1308 permitted "Aymer de Archiaco" to grant parts of the manors of Wolveton, Dorset, Midsummer Norton, Somerset, and Luton, Bedfordshire to "Joan de Vivonia and Reginald her son for their live
2 CONC s, with remainder to the latter’s son John"[981].] 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)         SIMON d’Archiac (-9 May [1324/26], bur Saintes).  Canon at Saintes.  Archbishop of Vienne 1319.  Cardinal 1320.  Duchesne records that Cardinal d’Archiac made his testament at Avignon 5 May 1323 but comments that “[il] 
2 CONC n’est pas venu jusqu’à nous”[982].  Duchesne cites the necrology of Sainte-Chapelle which records the death “Non Mai” of “domini cardinalis d’Archiac”[983]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT d)         GUILLAUME d’Archiac .  Monk. 
2 CONT
2 CONT e)         AIMERY d’Archiac . 
2 CONT
2 CONT f)          ANNE d’Archiac (-before 1316).  m as his first wife, SIMON [IV] Seigneur de Lezay, son of [SIMON [III] Seigneur de Lezay & his wife --- de Vivonne] (-1331 or after). 
