1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Medilands (''9 Mar 2022'') [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/brittcope.htm#AlainVitreDinanB J. Seigneurs de Dinan (Seigneurs de Vitré)]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/brittnpr.htm#AlainVitreDinanA '''ALAIN de Vitré'''], son of ROBERT Seigneur de Vitré & his wife Emma de Dinan (-before Oct 1200).  "Rollandus de Dinanno" granted property to Sauvigny with the conse
2 CONC nt of "Alano de Vitreio nepote meo", stating that the latter was his heir, by undated charter[772].  He adopted the name "de Dinan" as heir to his maternal uncle.  '''Seigneur de Dinan.'''  "Andreas de Vitreio" donated property to
2 CONC  Sauvigny, for the souls of "patris mei Roberti et matris mee Emme et uxoris mee Mathildis", with the consent of "Mathildis uxor mea et fratres mei Alanus et Robertus", by charter dated to [1173/84][773].  "Andreas dominus Vitrei"
2 CONC  donated property to Sauvigny, with the consent of "fratribus meis Alano, Roberto, Joscelino", by charter dated to [1175/84][774]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' as her '''first husband''', [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/brittnpr.htm#ClemenceFougeresdied1252 '''CLEMENCE de Fougères'''], daughter of GUILLAUME de Fougères & his wife Agatha du Hommet (-1252).  The primary source whi
2 CONC ch confirms her first marriage has not yet been identified.   She '''married secondly''' (before 7 Oct 1200) as his second wife, [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL.htm#RanulfChesterdied1232 '''Ranulf "d
2 CONC e Blundeville" Earl of Chester'''].  The Annales Cestrienses record in 1200 that “Rannulphus comes Cestrie”, having left “comitssa Britannie...Constancia”, married “filiam Radulphi de Feugis”[775].  King John confirmed "manerio de
2 CONC  Belinton" made by "Gaufr de Fulgeriis" to "R. com Cestr…in maritagio cum Clementia sorore sua" by charter dated 29 May 1204[776].  The Annals of Burton record the death “post Natale Domini” in 1252 of “Clementia comitissa de Repe
2 CONC ndun relicta…Ranulfi quondam comitis Cestriæ”[777]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''Alain & his wife had one child:''' 
2 CONT >1. '''GERVAISE de Vitré''' (-[1235/41]).  Vicomtesse de Dinan.  "Juhellus dominus Meduanæ et Dinani…Gervasia uxor mea filia Alani de Dinan…Isabella mater mea" founded the abbey of Fontaine-Daniel by charter dated 19 May 1205[778]
2 CONC .  "Juhel seigneur de Mayenne" donated property to the priory of Fontaine-Daniel, for the soul of "Gervaise sa femme", by charter dated 12 Feb 1207, witnessed by "…Isabelle de Mayenne…"[779].  "Juhellus de Meduana…cum assensu…Gerv
2 CONC asie uxoris mee" confirmed the donation of property to Craon Bonshommes made by "Stephanum de Chastelou et eius uxorem" by charter dated 1210[780].  "Juhellus Meduane et Dinanni dominus" donated property to Vieuville, with the con
2 CONC sent of "Gervasia uxore mea...filiabus meis Isabel et Margarita et Johanna", by charter dated 1212[781].  The obituary of Craon Bonshommes records the death 12 Apr of "dominus Juhellus de Meduana dominus Meduane et Dinani fundator
2 CONC  prioratus de Monteguidonis", adding that he donated property with the consent of "Gervasie uxoris sue filie et heredis Theobaldi de Dinan"[782].  "Richardus Maresschallus dominus Dinanni et Gervasia eius uxor" confirmed donations
2 CONC  to the abbey of Beaulieu by charter dated 1224[783].  "Henricus de Avalgor, filius Alani comitis…et Margarita uxor mea" renewed a donation of property to the abbey of Bon-Repos by "Gervasia domina Dinani", for the soul of "bone m
2 CONC emorie Gaufridi vicecomitis de Rohan quondam mariti sui", by charter dated 1229[784].  "Gervasia domina de Dynan" confirmed donations by "bone memorie Juhelli de Meduana quondam mariti nostri" to the abbey of Saint-Aubin-des-Bois 
2 CONC by charter dated 1235[785].  "Gervasia domina Dynanni" donated property to Saint-Aubin-des-Bois after the death of "bone memorie Richardi Marischallis, quondam mariti mei" by charter dated 1236[786].  Her date of death is confirme
2 CONC d by the charter dated 1241 under which "Droco de Melloto, Locharam et Meduane dominus" [her son-in-law] wrote to "fratri suo domino Henrico de Avalgor", naming "bone memorie domine Gervasie"[787]. '''m firstly''' (before 1189) [h
2 CONC ttp://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/mainnob.htm#JuhaelMayennedied1220 '''JUHEL Seigneur de Mayenne'''], son of GEOFFROY Seigneur de Mayenne & his second wife Isabelle de Meulan (-killed in battle 2 or 4 May 1220, bur Fontaine-Daniel). 
2 CONC  '''m secondly''' (after 4 May 1220) as his second wife, [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/brittnpr.htm#GeoffroyIRohandied1221 '''GEOFFROY (I) Vicomte de Rohan'''], son of ALAIN [IV] Vicomte de Rohan & his wife Mabile de Fougères (
2 CONC -15 Sep 1221).  '''m thirdly''' (before Jan 1224) [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL1.htm#RicahrdMarshalPembrokedied1234 '''RICHARD MarshaL'''], son of WILLIAM Marshal Earl of Pembroke & his wife Isabel
2 CONC  Ctss of Pembroke (-Kilkenny Castle 16 Apr 1234, bur Kilkenny, Church of the Franciscans).  He succeeded as Seigneur de Dinan in 1224, de iure uxoris[788].  He succeeded his brother in 1231 as Earl of Pembroke, hereditary Master M
2 CONC arshal.
