1 NOTE {geni:about_me} RAOUL de Roye .  Goethals records his parentage without citing the source which confirms the information[894].  Seigneur de la Ferté en Ponthieu, de iure uxoris[895].  m MARIE de Ville, daughter of ---.  Père Ansel
2 CONC me names her as the wife of Raoul de Roye but cites no primary source[896].  Goethals says that her father was “seigneur de Ville-sur-Illon” without citing the source which confirms the information[897].  Raoul & his wife had two 
2 CONC children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >*i)          MATHIEU [I] de Roye (-after Jul 1280).  Seigneur de la Ferté en Ponthieu.  '''m as her first husband, JEANNE de Vendeuil, daughter of CLAREMBAUD Seigneur de Vendeuil & his wife --- (-after 1319).  She married secondl
2 CONC y Jean [III] de Nesle Seigneur de Falvy.'''  “Mathieu de Roye chevalier Seigneur de la Ferté et de Vendeuil et…Jeanne sa femme dame de Vendeuil” settled a dispute with the convent of Saint-Nicolas or Bos in the bishopric of Laon c
2 CONC oncerning rights over “Choegny” by charter dated Jul 1280 which names “messire Huon de Vendeuil et messire Clerembaut”[898].  A document dated 1310 records a settlement between “domicellam Margaretam de Pinquigniaco” and “Ioannam 
2 CONC de Vendolio relictam defuncti Mathei de Roya militis”, which names “defuncti Mathei de Roya iunioris filii procreati ex eis...domicellæ Mariæ filiæ dictæ Ioannæ et dicti defuncti Mathei quondam mariti eiusdem”[899].  Her second ma
2 CONC rriage is confirmed by the charter dated May 1324 which named “Jeanne jadis Dame de Vendeuil mere Jehan de Fallevi chevalier hoir à present de ladite Dame” and required “[le]dit Iehan de Fallevi” to make payments to “Marie de la F
2 CONC reté sa suer et au Seigneur de Loques son mary”[900].  Mathieu & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>*(1)       MATHIEU [II] de Roye .  Seigneur de la Ferté en Ponthieu.  A document dated 1310 records a settlement between “domicellam Margaretam de Pinquigniaco” and “Ioannam de Vendolio relictam defuncti Mathei de Roya militis”,
2 CONC  which names “defuncti Mathei de Roya iunioris filii procreati ex eis...domicellæ Mariæ filiæ dictæ Ioannæ et dicti defuncti Mathei quondam mariti eiusdem”[901].  m (Apr 1291) MARGUERITE de Picquigny, daughter of JEAN de Picquigny
2 CONC  Vidame d’Amiens & his wife Marguerite de Beaumetz (-after 16 Nov 1343).  A document dated 1310 records a settlement between “domicellam Margaretam de Pinquigniaco” and “Ioannam de Vendolio relictam defuncti Mathei de Roya militis
2 CONC ”, which names “defuncti Mathei de Roya iunioris filii procreati ex eis...domicellæ Mariæ filiæ dictæ Ioannæ et dicti defuncti Mathei quondam mariti eiusdem”[902].  Mathieu [II] & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>*(a)       ELEONORE de Roye (-[7 Jan 1329/1333]).  Her marriage and family origin are confirmed by the marriage contract between "Iehan de Chasteillon chevalier Sires de Gandelus, de la Ferté et de Marigny et Lienor de Roye sa 
2 CONC fame...Gauchier leur fils ainsné" and "Damoiselle Jeanne filhe de...Iehan de Guines Vicomte de Miaux et Sire de Fertez Ancoul et Gauchier et de feu Madame Jehanne de Chantilly iadis sa fame", dated Sep 1323[903].  Dame de la Ferté
2 CONC  en Ponthieu.  A document of the Parlement de Paris dated 7 Jan 1329 records the rejection of the claim by “Jean de Chatillon chevalier et Aliénor sa femme, seigneurs de La Ferté en Ponthieu, d’Yaucourt et de Dury en Vermandois” f
2 CONC or a fifth part of the dower of “Marguerite de Picquigny damoiselle de La Ferté, veuve de Mathieu de Roye et mère d’Aliénor”[904].  Duchesne records a charter dated 1333 in which Jean donates property for the souls of “sa...compag
2 CONC ne defunte et de leurs enfans”[905].  m as his first wife, JEAN de Châtillon Seigneur de Gandelus, son of GAUCHER [V] de Châtillon Comte de Porcien & his first wife Isabelle de Dreux (-1363, bur Cerfroy). 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>*(b)       BEATRIX de Roye .  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>*(2)       MARIE de Roye .  A document dated 1310 records a settlement between “domicellam Margaretam de Pinquigniaco” and “Ioannam de Vendolio relictam defuncti Mathei de Roya militis”, which names “defuncti Mathei de Roya iuni
2 CONC oris filii procreati ex eis...domicellæ Mariæ filiæ dictæ Ioannæ et dicti defuncti Mathei quondam mariti eiusdem”[906].  Dame de Vendeuil.  A charter dated May 1324 named “Jeanne jadis Dame de Vendeuil mere Jehan de Fallevi cheval
2 CONC ier hoir à present de ladite Dame” and required “[le]dit Iehan de Fallevi” to make payments to “Marie de la Freté sa suer et au Seigneur de Loques son mary”[907].  m GUILLAUME [IV] de Béthune Seigneur de Locres et de Hebuterne, so
2 CONC n of GUILLAUME [III] de Béthune Seigneur de Locres et de Herbuterne & his wife Jeanne de Nesle dite de Falvy (-after 1310). 
2 CONT
2 CONT >*ii)         MARIE de Roye (-13 Mar ----).  The executors of “domini Auberti de Hangesto” claimed against “comitem Vindocinensem” for “dotalicio comitisse uxoris sue” dated 1260[908].  Her third marriage is confirmed by the necro
2 CONC logy of Saint-Nicolas de Courville which records the death “V Non Mai“ of "dominus Johannes de Veteriponte miles junior” and his donation for the anniversaries of “patris et matris eiusdem necnon et domini Yvonis condam fratris su
2 CONC i” made “Curveville in castello...in presencia nobilis domine domine de Vindocino domine de Curvavilla uxoris eiusdem...anno LXXI die mercurii post Concepcionem beate Marie Virginis” [1270/71][909].  A charter dated 1272 records a
2 CONC  judgment against “B. comitem Vindocinensem” and after his death “dominam Mariam comitissam Vindocinensem, ratione liberorum suorum” relating to the capture of four men in the land of Sentier priory[910].  The necrology of Vendôme
2 CONC  La Trinité records the death "V Non Mar" of "Maria comitissa"[911].  The necrology of Saint-Nicolas de Courville records the death “III Id Mar“ of "Marie domine de Curveville condam comitisse Vindocinensis et matris Yvonis domini
2 CONC  Curveville militis” and the donation for whom of “annui redditus super preposituram Curveville, ad festum beati Remigii”[912].  m firstly AUBERT [IV] de Hangest Seigneur de Genlis, son of [AUBERT [III] Seigneur de Genlis & his wi
2 CONC fe Beatrix de Châtillon] (-before 1259).  m secondly ([before 1259]) BOUCHARD [VIII] Comte de Vendôme, son of PIERRE Comte de Vendôme & his wife Jeanne de Mayenne (-[15 May 1271], bur St Georges de Vendôme).  m thirdly ([15 May/9 
2 CONC Dec] 1271) JEAN de Vieuxpont Seigneur de Courville, son of ROBERT de Vieuxpont Seigneur de Courville & his wife Isabelle de Maillebois (-3 May ----).
2 CONT
