1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joan de Munchensy, Countess of Pembroke was born on 1230 in Pembroke Castle, Pembroke, Pembrokeshire, Wales to Sir Warin de Munchensy, Lord of Swanscombe and Joan Marshal de Munchensy.  Joan married Sir William de 
2 CONC Valance, Earl of Pembroke, Knight on 1248 in Pembroke Castle, Pembroke, Pembrokeshire, Wales and had 7 children:  Agnes de Valance; John de Valance; Margaret de Valance; William de Valance, Sire de Montignac and Bellac; Joan de Va
2 CONC lance; Isabel de Valance; and Aymer de Valance, 2nd Earl of Pembroke.  She passed away AFTER September 20, 1307 and is buried in Swanscombe, Dartford, Kent, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan de Munchensy de Valance is my 26th great aunt. She is my 21st GGrandmother
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
