2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ='''WILLIAM DE WARENNE, son and heir apparent.'''=
2 CONT  In 1276 he agreed that his father might at his death dispose of the Earl's lands in Norfolk. In 1285 he was knighted at Winchester; and in the same year obtained quittance from the common summons in Essex, Bucks and Norfolk. He m
2 CONC arried, probably in June 1285, Joan, daughter of Robert (DE VERE), 5th EARL OF OXFORD, by Alice, daughter and heir of Gilbert DE SANFORD. He died v.p. 15 December 1286, having attended a tournament at Croydon, where he is said to 
2 CONC have been ambushed and cruelly slain by his rivals. His widow died on or before 23 November 1293, and was buried before the high altar at Lewes. [Complete Peerage XII/1:507, (transcribed by Dave Utzinger)]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT William de Warenne, Knight, son and heir of John de Warrenne and Alice de Lusignan, was born 15 Jan 1255/6 at Warren, Sussex, England. He married Joan de Vere about 10 June 1285. She is the daughter of Robert de Vere, Knight, and 
2 CONC Alice de Sanford. They had one son, John, and one daughter, Alice. "Sir William was knighted at Winchester in 1285." He was ambushed and slain by his rivals after a tournament at Croyden 15 Dec 1286.
2 CONT Name
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: William de Warenne, Knight, did not ever inherit the title of Earl of Surrey, because he died before his father. His father was the 7th Earl of Surrey and his son was the 8th Earl of Surrey.
2 CONT Father: John DE WARENNE, 7th Earl of Surrey, b. abt. 1231, Warren, Sussex, England. d. abt. 1304 Mother: Alice (Lusignan) DE WARENNE, b. abt. 1224, of Arundel, Sussex, England. d. aft. 9 Feb 1256
