1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/burgkbresse.htm#BeatrixColignydied1240
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         BEATRIX de Coligny ([1194/95 or soon after]-[1240/Jan 1242]).  "Albertus de Turre filius Alberti de Turre et Comitissæ filiæ Roberti comitis Arverniæ" confirmed donations to the Chartreuse de Portes by "Hugonis de Colin
2 CONC iaco" on the occasion of his marriage to "filiæ eius Beatricis" by undated charter[186].  Her birth date is estimated bearing in mind her mother’s age when she married Beatrix’s father.  "Albertus de Turre, dominus de Turre et Col
2 CONC igniaco et Beatrix uxor mea et filii" confirmed purchases of property by the bishop of Belley by charter dated 1228[187].  Dame de Malleval et de Rochechaume.  She was named as deceased in her husband’s donation dated Jan 1241 (O.
2 CONC S.).  The estimated birth date of her son Humbert suggests that Béatrix died giving birth to him.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (before 4 May 1220) ALBERT [III] Seigneur de la Tour, son of ALBERT [II] Seigneur de la Tour & his wife Marie d'Auvergne ([1180/85]-[Apr 1259/Jun 1260]).  Albert [III] & his wife had seven children: 
