1 OCCU Baron de La Tour-du-Pin, Sénéchal du royaume d'Arles-Vienne
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/burgkvien.htm#AlbertIIITourPindied1264 [March 2021]
2 CONT
2 CONT  Eldest son of Albert II de la Tour du Pin and Marie d'Auvergne
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         '''ALBERT [III]''' de la Tour-du-Pin ([1180/85]-[Apr 1259/Jun 1260]).  He is referred to but not named in his father’s [1190] testament, when he was under age.  "Albertus dominus de Turre…Albertus filius meus" donated p
2 CONC roperty to the priory of Ynimont by charter dated 1202[2118].  The likely birth date of his wife Beatrix suggests that Albert [III] was probably still a child at the time of his first betrothal, suggesting his birth in [1190].  "A
2 CONC lbertus de Turre filius Alberti de Turre et Comitissæ filiæ Roberti comitis Arverniæ" confirmed donations to the Chartreuse de Portes by "Hugonis de Coliniaco" on the occasion of his marriage to "filiæ eius Beatricis" by undated c
2 CONC harter[2119].  Seigneur de la Tour-du-Pin.  Seneschal of the kingdom of Arles and Vienne.  "Albertus de Turre, dominus de Turre et Coligniaco et Beatrix uxor mea et filii" confirmed purchases of property by the bishop of Belley by
2 CONC  charter dated 1228[2120].  “Albert seigneur de la Tour et son fils Albert” donated revenue to Notre-Dame d’Ambronay, for the soul of “leur épouse et mère Béatrix“, by charter dated Jan 1241 (O.S.)[2121].  “Hugo...Claromontanus ep
2 CONC iscopus et Humbertus dominus Bellijoci, et Arbertus dominus de Turre, et Guido archidiaconus Lugdunensis, et Arbertus de Turre, et Hugo senescalcus Lugdunensis fratres” agreed an alliance under a charter dated Sep 1246[2122].  "Al
2 CONC bers Segnor de la Tor et Albers son filz" swore homage to "Monsegnor Perron de Savoye" by charter dated Sep 1250[2123].  “Albert le jeune seigneur de la Tour et de Coligny”, on the advice of “son père Albert de la Tour, de ses frè
2 CONC res Hugues de la Tour sénéchal de Lyon, et Humbert de la Tour” granted freedoms to his town of Treffort en Bresse by charter dated Apr 1259[2124].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[Betrothed]''' (conditional contract 21 Nov 1198) to --- de Bressieux, daughter of AYMAR de Bressieux & his wife Aynarde --- (-after 1198).  The contract of marriage between "Dom. Aynarda quondam uxor Audemari de Brisseu et mat
2 CONC er Audemari pueri" and "Arberto de Turre…filiam suam" is dated 1198, and provides that if the prospective bridegroom died before the marriage, "Arbertus filius Arberti" would marry "sororem dicti Audemari"[2125].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (before 4 May 1220) BEATRIX de Coligny, daughter of HUGUES Seigneur de Coligny-le-Neuf & his wife Beatrix d'Albon Dauphine de Viennois, Ctss d'Albon ([1194/95 or soon after]-[1240/Jan 1242]).  "Albertus de Turre filius Alb
2 CONC erti de Turre et Comitissæ filiæ Roberti comitis Arverniæ" confirmed donations to the Chartreuse de Portes by "Hugonis de Coliniaco" on the occasion of his marriage to "filiæ eius Beatricis" by undated charter[2126].  Her birth da
2 CONC te is estimated bearing in mind her mother’s age when she married Beatrix’s father.  "Albertus de Turre, dominus de Turre et Coligniaco et Beatrix uxor mea et filii" confirmed purchases of property by the bishop of Belley by chart
2 CONC er dated 1228[2127].  She was named as deceased in her husband’s donation dated Jan 1241 (O.S.), cited above.  The estimated birth date of her son Humbert suggests that Béatrix died giving birth to him.  
2 CONT
2 CONT  Albert [III] & his wife had seven children: 
2 CONT *a)         ALBERT [IV] de la Tour-du-Pin (-before Feb 1269).  "Hugo de Turre, abbas Claromontensis, et Guido frater eiusdem, canonicus Claromontensis" noted a donation to Cluny by charter dated 13 Oct 1238, which names “dominum A
2 CONC lbertum de Turre patrem nostrum, et Albertum filium eius fratrem nostrum…”[2128].  “Albert seigneur de la Tour et son fils Albert” donated revenue to Notre-Dame d’Ambronay, for the soul of “leur épouse et mère Béatrix“, by charter
2 CONC  dated Jan 1241 (O.S.)[2129].  “Hugo...Claromontanus episcopus et Humbertus dominus Bellijoci, et Arbertus dominus de Turre, et Guido archidiaconus Lugdunensis, et Arbertus de Turre, et Hugo senescalcus Lugdunensis fratres” agreed
2 CONC  an alliance under a charter dated Sep 1246[2130].  Seigneur de Coligny: “Albertus de Turre dominus Coloniaci, filius Alberti” renounced rights “super manso de Faye...et...de la Barandonire” in favour of “domus hospitalis Jerosoli
2 CONC mitani de les Foillies” by charter dated Feb 1246 (O.S.?)[2131].  The testament of “G. de Turre archidiaconus Lugdunensis”, dated 24 Feb 1249 (O.S.), bequeathed property to “Hugonem senescalcum Lugdunensem...Humberti nepoti meo...
2 CONC frater suus...nepotem meum Albertum...”[2132].  "Albers Segnor de la Tor et Albers son filz" swore homage to "Monsegnor Perron de Savoye" by charter dated Sep 1250[2133].  Seigneur de la Tour-du-Pin.  “Albert le jeune seigneur de 
2 CONC la Tour et de Coligny”, on the advice of “son père Albert de la Tour, de ses frères Hugues de la Tour sénéchal de Lyon, et Humbert de la Tour” granted freedoms to his town of Treffort en Bresse by charter dated Apr 1259[2134].  "A
2 CONC lbertus dominus de Turre filius quondam domini Alberti de Turre" confirmed the grant of sheep grazing rights to Grenoble Saint-Robert made by "Albertus quondam dominus de Turre avus noster et dictus dominus Albertus pater noster" 
2 CONC by charter dated 2 Jan 1265[2135].  The Feb 1269 charter of his wife quoted below implies that Albert was deceased at the time.  m ([Sep 1250/Mar 1251]) ADALASIA Fiesco, daughter of [TEODORO/OPIZZONE] Fiesco [Conte di Lavagna] & h
2 CONC is wife Simona --- (-after May 1273).  Matthew Paris records that Pope Innocent IV arranged the marriage of his niece to "domino de Tur de Pin" in 1251 and that he accepted his bride "non ratione personæ muliebris, sed pecuniæ eam
2 CONC  concomitantis"[2136].  Her mother’s name is confirmed by the reference to her mother in the May 1273 testament quoted below.  On the basis of the primary sources currently identified, her father could have been either Teodoro Fie
2 CONC schi or his brother Opizzone Fieschi, whose wives were both named Simona.  The marriage presumably formed part of arrangements when Albert [III] swore homage to Pierre de Savoie in Sep 1250 for la Tour (see above).  “Adalasia dame
2 CONC  de la Tour” placed under her protection “des hommes de la chartreuse” at the request of the prior of Portes by charter dated Mar 1251[2137].  “Adalasia domina de Turre” took under her protection “tres homines...ad Chalona...” by 
2 CONC charter dated Dec 1251 and others by charter dated Mar 1252[2138].  "Humbertus de Turre Delphinus Viennæ" confirmed the rights of "fratrum nostrum Dom. Albertum quondam dominum de Turre et de Coliniaco…dom. Alisiæ quondam uxori su
2 CONC æ" in "castrum sancti Saturnini…villam de Brango…villæ et castri Crimiaci…" as well as in all property (unspecified) which Alix had acquired from "Guefredo de Vireu domicello quondam filio Dom. Alberti de Vireu militis defuncti et
2 CONC  Berengariæ eiusdem G. matris, quæ acquisita sunt in mandamento castri de Turre" and from "Giroudo Vimont quondam clerico", by charter dated Feb 1269, which also provides if "Alisiæ ad secundas nuptias convolaret"[2139].  The fami
2 CONC ly connections, if any, between Adalasia and Guifred de Virieu and Géraud Vimont are not specified in the document.  In the case of the former, it seems unlikely that he was Adalasia’s first husband as the document refers to the p
2 CONC ossibility of her "secundas nuptias" not "tertias".  In any case, Guifred de Virieu is named in a document dated 1267 (although it appears that he died before Feb 1269)[2140], when it is likely that Alix was already married to Alb
2 CONC ert [IV] de la Tour-du-Pin.  Maybe they were related to Adalasia through her mother.  The testament of "Adalasiæ relictæ Alberti junioris domini de Turre Pini et de Coloniaco", dated May 1273, bequeathed property to "Humberto de T
2 CONC urre fratri domini mei et mariti mei…dominæ Simondæ…matri meæ…domine Comitisse del Borget consanguinee mee…Thome et Amedeo de Sabaudia filiis eiusdem…Hugoni de Turre senescallo Lugdun."[2141].  Could "…domine Comitisse del Borget 
2 CONC consanguinee mee… " in this document be Simone [Sibylle] Dame de Bâgé, wife of Amédée de Savoie whose mother was Adalasia’s sister? 
2 CONT
2 CONT *b)         MARIE de la Tour-du-Pin (-after Feb 1266).  The marriage contract between "Willelmi comitis Gebenn…R. filium" and "Guigonis Dalphini Vienn. et Albonensis…dominam M. filiam domini A. de Turre" is dated 8 Jun 1241[2142].
2 CONC   Dame de Varey, de Vaux et de Saint-Sorlin.  “Maria comitissa Gebennensis et domina de Varey” confirmed the donation to the Chartreuse at Meria in Bugey made by “bonæ memoriæ Hugo dominus Coloniaci quondam pater [error for avus] 
2 CONC noster” with the consent of “Willelmus dominus Coloniaci frater quondam dicti domini Hugonis”, by charter dated Feb 1266[2143].  m (contract 8 Jun 1241) RODOLPHE de Genève, son of GUILLAUME [II] Comte de Genève & his [second] wife
2 CONC  Alix --- ([before 1215]-29 May 1265).  He succeeded in 1253 as Comte de Genève. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *c)         HUGUES de la Tour-du-Pin (-after 1289).  "Hugo de Turre, abbas Claromontensis, et Guido frater eiusdem, canonicus Claromontensis" noted a donation to Cluny by charter dated 13 Oct 1238, which names “dominum Albertum de
2 CONC  Turre patrem nostrum, et Albertum filium eius fratrem nostrum…”[2144].  “Hugo...Claromontanus episcopus et Humbertus dominus Bellijoci, et Arbertus dominus de Turre, et Guido archidiaconus Lugdunensis, et Arbertus de Turre, et Hu
2 CONC go senescalcus Lugdunensis fratres” agreed an alliance under a charter dated Sep 1246[2145].  Under her testament dated Mar 1249, "Alays de Roians, domina castri Sancti Johannis de Bornay, uxor quondam nobilis viri dom Ose Sicce" 
2 CONC bequeathes property to "…Ugone nepoti meo de Turre, senescalco Lugdunensi" and also names "fratre meo dome Alberto de Turre"[2146].  The testament of “G. de Turre archidiaconus Lugdunensis”, dated 24 Feb 1249 (O.S.), bequeathed pr
2 CONC operty to “Hugonem senescalcum Lugdunensem...Humberti nepoti meo...frater suus...nepotem meum Albertum...”[2147].  “Albert le jeune seigneur de la Tour et de Coligny”, on the advice of “son père Albert de la Tour, de ses frères Hu
2 CONC gues de la Tour sénéchal de Lyon, et Humbert de la Tour” granted freedoms to his town of Treffort en Bresse by charter dated Apr 1259[2148].  “Drodonet seigneur de Beauvoir-de-Marc, fils de Guillaume sr dud. lieu” granted “[le] ch
2 CONC âteau...de St-Jean-de-Bournay” to “son cousin Hugues de la Tour sénéchal de Lyon” by charter dated 1 Apr 1278[2149]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *d)         GUY de la Tour-du-Pin (-1286).  "Hugo de Turre, abbas Claromontensis, et Guido frater eiusdem, canonicus Claromontensis" noted a donation to Cluny by charter dated 13 Oct 1238, which names “dominum Albertum de Turre pa
2 CONC trem nostrum, et Albertum filium eius fratrem nostrum…”[2150].  Bishop of Clermont .  The epitaph of "Guido de Turre 37 episcopus Arverniæ" records his death in 1286[2151]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *e)         BEATRIX de la Tour-du-Pin (-after 21 Sep 1280).  A charter dated 8 Sep 1276 acknowledged receipt of money from "Beatrix de la Tour, femme de Guillaume de Roussillon sire d’Annonay, alors outre-mer" by "Guillaume abbé d
2 CONC e Saint-Pierre"[2152].  Her parentage and marriage are confirmed by the charter dated 21 Sep 1280 under which "Beatrix de Turre domina Rossillonis et Annoniaci, relicta bonæ memoriæ Dom. Willelmi de Rossillone" donated property "i
2 CONC n parrochia de la Versin" to the Cartusians to found the abbey of Sainte-Croix[2153].  m GUILLAUME Seigneur de Roussillon et d’Annonay, son of ARTAUD [IV] Seigneur de Roussillon & his wife M--- [de Genève] ([before 1239]-Château d
2 CONC 'Annonay 21 Dec 1277, bur Notre-Dame [Vienne]). 
2 CONT
2 CONT *f)          ALIX de la Tour-du-Pin (-after 1289).  Her parentage is indicated by the presence of her brother Humbert in the Apr 1274 charter of her daughter Catherine.  “Humbertus dominus Montislupelli” granted privileges to Mont
2 CONC luel, with the consent of “...Guidonis de Montelupello domini de Castellione in Chautagnia...fratris [nostri]...domine Alasie domine Montislupelli uxoris nostre”, by charter dated Mar 1276[2154].  An inscription in the church of M
2 CONC ontluel St Barthélemy records the church’s foundation in 1289 by “dominum Humbertum dominum Montislupelli et...dominam Alaysiam de Turre eius uxorem”[2155].  Dame de Verfieu.  m HUMBERT [II] Seigneur de Montluel, son of PIERRE [I]
2 CONC  Seigneur de Montluel & his wife ---  (-after Apr 1289). 
2 CONT
2 CONT *g)         HUMBERT [I] de la Tour-du-Pin ([1240]-monastère du Val-Sainte-Marie 12 Apr 1307, bur Val-Sainte-Marie).  The testament of “G. de Turre archidiaconus Lugdunensis”, dated 24 Feb 1249 (O.S.), bequeathed property to “Hugon
2 CONC em senescalcum Lugdunensem...Humberti nepoti meo...frater suus...nepotem meum Albertum...”[2156].  His parentage is confirmed by the testament of his sister-in-law "Adalasiæ relictæ Alberti junioris domini de Turre Pini et de Colo
2 CONC niaco", dated May 1273, which bequeathed property to "Humberto de Turre fratri domini mei et mariti mei…"[2157].  Seigneur de la Tour-du-Pin.  Seigneur de Coligny: “Humbertus dominus Montislupelli” granted privileges to Montluel, 
2 CONC with the consent of “...domini nostri...Humberti domini de Turre et de Cologniaco...”, by charter dated Mar 1276[2158].  He was installed as Dauphin de Viennois, Comte d'Albon at Grenoble, église collégiale de Saint-André, 3 Oct 1
2 CONC 282.  Later in life, he became a monk at the Chartreuse Monastery of Val-Sainte-Marie.  -        DAUPHINS de VIENNOIS. 
