2 CONT
2 CONT GUILLEN Ramón de Montcada, son of GUILLEN de Montcada [II] Señor de Montcada y Vic & his wife Marie de Béarn (1166-mid-1224, bur Sainte-Marie d'Oloron).  He inherited the Montcada patrimony under the 1173 will of his grandfather. 
2 CONC  "Wastonius III filius Marie" and “Willelmus R frater memorati Gastonis” confirmed donations made by “predecessorum meorum” by undated charters[110].  It appears that he was responsible for the murder in 1194 of his wife's uncle B
2 CONC erenguer de Vilademuls, Archbishop of Tarragona, who was closely associated with don Alfonso II King of Aragon, Conde de Barcelona, in his struggle with the Cabrera-Castellbò party of which Guillem Ramon was a member.  Although no
2 CONC t directly punished for the crime, he spent much of the following 20 years in exile.  He succeeded his brother in 1214 as GUILLAUME [I] Vicomte de Béarn.  He resettled in Catalonia in [1215], seeking penance in Rome[111].  "W. R…v
2 CONC icecomes Bearnensis" wrote to Henry III King of England, dated to [1219], assuring him of the loyalty of the citizens of Bayonne[112].  "Guillermus Raymundi de Montecatano vicecomes Bearnensis" issued a charter for the church of T
2 CONC arragona dated 27 Feb 1223, which names "Guillermi filii mei" and refers to the testament of "bonæ memoriæ fratris mei Gastonis vicecomitis Bearnensis"[113]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (before 1185) [as her first husband,] GUILLEMA de Castellvell, daughter of GUILLEM [V] Senyor de Castellvell de Rosanes & his wife --- (-[1226/28]).  Her parentage and marriage are confirmed by the Annals of Surita which r
2 CONC ecord that her son "Don Guillen de Moncada, hijo de Don Guillen Ramon de Moncada y de Donna Guillelma de Casteluell, que caso con la viscondessa de Bearne" was not present at the battle of Muret in 1213 but sent messengers to the 
2 CONC king[114].  She was abandoned by her husband and married secondly (bigamously, 1202) as his first wife, Aimery [III] Vicomte de Narbonne.  She returned to Catalonia after separating from her second husband in 1208[115].  She succe
2 CONC eded her brother in 1205 as Senyora de Castellvell de Rosanes, Mara, El Far, Pontous, Benviure, Llvaneres, Olesa, Voltrera. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mistress''' (1): NAVARRA, daughter of ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Guillaume & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Guillaume [I] had four illegitimate children by Mistress (1):   
