1 CONC  the Mourne Mountains.  He pursued the de Lacys and their startle d allies north to Downpatrick and then to Carrickfergus.  He took Carr ickfergus and seized the lands of the Lacys and banished the Earl of U lster, built several f
1 CONC ortresses and appointed sheriffs and other offic ers to carry out the English system of law.  By August 1210,  John ha d landed at Fishguard, Pembrokeshire and was back in England.  John's distrust of his barons and his animosityl
