0 @N6000000007329549219@ NOTE [The Saxon & Norman Kings, by Christopher Brooke] (1199-1216).  [] date
1 CONT of accession 1199. House of Plantagenet.  [T. Webster, fidonet, Aug '95]
1 CONT John LACKLAND, PLANTAGENET King.  [John Byl, byl - at - twu.ca] Does
1 CONT anyone know much about the   ancestors  and  descendents of the famous
1 CONT St. William of Orange, marquess of   Septimania  (790-806), cousin of
1 CONT Charlemagne? Sir Anthony Wagner ('Pedigree  &   Progree')  suggest he was
1 CONT of Jewish descent (from the exilarchs from  babylon),   as well  as an
1 CONT ancestor of the English royal line through Isabel  of   Angouleme, wife
1 CONT of  King John of England. Is this all mere fantasy, or  is there some
1 CONT sound basis  to such claims?
1 CONT [In a previous article, tavenner -at- ux4.cso.uiuc.edu (Patrick
1 CONT Tavenner)  says: 'The post about the descendants of William the Conquerer
1 CONT renewed a  question  for me.  I have wondered about the wives, mistresses
1 CONT and   children of  John  Lackland, King of England.  Did he have any
1 CONT other bastard   children  besides  than Richard FitzRoy?  The following
1 CONT is the information that   I have  gathered so far.  Any additions,
1 CONT corrections, observations, or   speculations  would be welcome.
1 CONT John 'Lackland' King ENGLAND. B: 24 DEC 1167, Kings Manor  house,
1 CONT Oxford.  D: 19 OCT 1216, ,Newark,Nottingham. Bur: Cathedral, Worcester.
1 CONT FAMILY 1:  Isabel   FITZROBERT  B: ABT 1170, of,,Gloucest. D: 14 OCT
1 CONT 1217, dsp,   Kent.  Bur: Cathedral,Canterbury,Kent. M:29 Aug 1189,
1 CONT Marlborough,   Salisbury,  Wiltshire. Annuled: 1200.
1 CONT FAMILY 2:  Isabella de  TAILLEFER....  This is not an appropriate name.
1 CONT Taillefer, or something of the   sort, was  a  nickname of her father,
1 CONT and perhaps of other family members, but not   a  location. She should be
1 CONT called Isabelle d'Angouleme, or the like.
